{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters","id":998305,"title":"[OOC] (Promethean: The Created 2E) Muddy Waters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T10:41:51-07:00","id":998305,"title":"[OOC] (Promethean: The Created 2E) Muddy Waters","content":"<b><u>Muddy Waters</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Winnipeg the ruin, Winnipeg of the haunted past, </i><br /> <i>Winnipeg of murder and flames. </i><br /> <i>Winnipeg of cold and death, </i><br /> <i>Winnipeg of the hopeless, </i><br /> <i>Winnipeg the doomed.</i> <br /> \u2013Jonathan Ball, Preface to The Shadow Over Portage and Main<br /> <br /> Once upon a time, it was marked \u2018Chicago of the North\u2019 and it was supposed to be the first city in North America to hit a population of a million, but it was eaten out by corruption, and then crippled by the following strikes. It\u2019s a patchwork city, cobbled together from the corpses of several others, and assembled around the beating heart of three mighty rivers. It\u2019s the Heart of the Continent, born in bloody revolution, and steeped in fire and blood ever since.<br /> <br /> It is a city of extremes.<br /> <br /> Extremes in temperature, extremes in relationships, extremes in arts.<br /> <br /> It has been called the most generous city in Canada, and also its most racist.<br /> It is home to fatalistic visionary artists who never get their careers off the prairie ground.<br /> Locals can\u2019t wait to get out of here, and visitors don\u2019t want to leave.<br /> <br /> You can make one thing into another in Winnipeg, and that\u2019s true alchemy.<br /> <br /> <b>Current Player Characters</b><br /> <b>1. </b>@Caladiru : Earth Crisis/Earth-Dies-Screaming/Earth, Recovering Centimanus<br /> <b>2. </b>@Wormwood : Mark 5, Hero with an \u2018F\u2019 in good<br /> <br /> <b>Created Winnipeg</b><br /> The \u2018Peg is, in many ways, a typical prairie city, a place of flat land and several rivers, the Red, the Seine, and the Assiniboine. Unfortunately, given the occasionally violent atmosphere of the city, more than one body has ended up in the muddy waters that the city is named after. For those who care to look, you can find gorgeous Chicago style and neoclassical architecture; however some spectacular postmodern buildings make occasional appearances in the cityscape.<br /> <br /> Everyone knows everyone in Winnipeg, fitting the Canadian stereotype of small, tight-knit population centers. If you say that you know someone in Winnipeg, a local speaking to you stands a good chance of knowing them. In an average city of this size, there\u2019s six degrees of separation. In Winnipeg there are only three. This means that word travels fast, and that any secrets that stay that way are because of a fierce sense of commitment and loyalty\u2026 or by the truly <i>bizarre </i>atmosphere in the city.<br /> <br /> Winnipeg is almost oppressive in its gothic supernatural airs and elemental, Lovecraftian, meteorological harshness. But more than that, a feeling of the uncanny, of the inhuman, lies over the city, stretching back as long as anyone can tell. In the first few decades of the 20<sup>th</sup> Century, it was the home of many prominent spiritualists, so much so that Arthur Conan Doyle came to visit them, and Henry Houdini came to discredit them. It\u2019s rather telling that neither individual spoke much about what they experienced. To this day, the city is a haven for mediums and psychics of all stripes.<br /> <br /> Everyone has a ghost story of some kind or another, and most major landmarks in Downtown Winnipeg are mentioned as being at least casually haunted. The Spirit Woods in the South End of the city are full of carvings that may or may not provide homes to beings of the <i>Hisil</i>, and one massive statue made from a dead tree named Mhitik appears to be both powerful and inhabited.<br /> <br /> Over the past several years, more and more Prometheans have decided to make Winnipeg a stop on their Pilgrimage. The mosaic of cultures, the presence of vibrant arts and culture instillations, and the Canadian Museum for Human Rights, has made it a veritable lab for learning about as many possible facets of humanity as you can.<br /> <br /> <b>Points of Interest</b><br /> The Manitoba Legislative Building is a masterwork of neoclassical architecture that was built using extremely precise occult geometry from several traditions, and is adorned with symbols from several different cultures- Greco-Roman, First Nations, Egyptian, and Roman Catholic -every single fixture and quirk in the building was chosen with symbolic intent, and to those in the know it positively <i>glows</i> with power. There are Athanors scorched into those stones. Decoding the building could unlock alchemical secrets untold.<br /> <br /> The Exchange District is a hub for artists, gourmands, and coffee connoisseurs. Once, it was the economic heart of the city, and now it is the cutting edge for arts and culture. Old vaulted passages of horse and carriage hide extensive Pilgrim marks, and the local graffiti artists have taken to using alchemical symbolism in their tags.<br /> <br /> The Fort Gary Hotel was built on the old grounds of Upper Fort Gary and is considered the most haunted building in the city.<br /> <br /> Elysium Social Club is the premier vehicle for Goth and EMB entertainment in Winnipeg. They regularly sponsor and host performances at different venues throughout the city, and those who know even the littlest bit about the supernatural get a kind of adrenaline rush from attending. Never know when one of the Kindred will come wafting out of the crowd.<br /> <br /> Elements Curiosity Shop is an occult bookstore mere steps away from the University of Winnipeg campus. Its owner is known for being able to pull strings and introduce customers to people a little more\u2026 involved than your run-of-the-mill psychic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:36:12-07:00","id":998342,"title":"","content":"Excited! Since you gave us an open-ended start and it's the first point of interest, I think Earth's going to take advantage of the fog to risk a trip to the Exchange District in search of pilgrim marks and other signs of occult interest. Mark 5 is welcome to join!<br /> <br /> Also, in another PBP game on these forums we keep track of resource stats and Conditions with this post header. It might be helpful to use it here too, or some other solution. You list what you have when the post starts, then indicate when you gain or spend stuff or charge an Alembic. <div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:51:14-07:00","id":998349,"title":"","content":"That most definitely works as a way of keeping track for things. Nice and concise. I'm planning on grounding the game with photography and news, at least for the portions set in Winnipeg. Hopefully that helps with the atmosphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:57:04-07:00","id":998354,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I appreciated the news stories! I might look around in Street View a little.<br /> <br /> Do you want to talk about instinctive Milestones and Pilgrimage planning now, or wait until we've gotten <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> in and maybe finished a chapter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-04-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:29:44-07:00","id":998381,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> No go ahead, I was just curious. And I haven't quite had the time to digest Promethean 2e yet. I may be looking for another game in January or so, once we've hit a good stride with The Supernal Suburbia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:29:09-07:00","id":998467,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> feel free to join us at any time.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> sure, let's start planning Earth's Pilgrimage now. What do you see as her major challenges on the road ahead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T17:24:24-07:00","id":998511,"title":"","content":"Ideas from the 5 Questions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>What sort of human do you want to be?</b><br /> &quot;Handsome, masculine, tall, I guess. Mostly I don't wanna need people to like me or care whether they respect me or not, because I'm so sure of who I am and where I'm supposed to be that I've got everything I need already. I want there to be no one I'd rather be than me.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Some minor Milestones here could be: presenting as a different gender and seeing how she likes it, meeting a trans or genderqueer human, talking to a First Nations human about their heritage, finding some quality or trait that she sincerely likes about herself, being told that she doesn't belong somewhere, remaining in some place or position despite someone telling her she shouldn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>How have humans taught you to fear and hate?</b><br /> &quot;I ain't afraid of humans, they're afraid of me. What would I be afraid of? Anyone who tries to fuck with me is gonna end up dead.<br /> <br /> I hate humans because they're beautiful to me. It's not even anger, they're just...there, in my brain, dancing and laughing and holding hands and shit. Not laughing at me, they don't care about me, I know that. Just being happy being themselves. Even when I was a Freak, they were still in my head, still beautiful. That's what got me out.<br /> <br /> I think the Principle created humans to show me what I can't have. What I can never have.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Minor or major milestone ideas: physically hurt a human for threatening her. Meet a human who isn't happy being themself. Feel sincere fear of a human. Meet a human who feels alienated from others. See two or more humans laughing together at the same thing. Meet a human whom she considers beautiful, and learn how they're flawed or their beauty isn't the whole story. Dance with humans. Have a human express that they care about her well-being. Ask a human why they think they exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>How did you split with your creator?</b> </div> </div> </div>Definitely a major or superlative Milestone here about facing her creator (if she's still alive) and making a choice about whether to continue their fight or find a way to resolve or transcend their mutual hatred. Maybe deciding whether or not she wants to create progeny after she had such a bad experience, that's also a universal Milestone though. Minor milestone: hear someone else tell a story in the Ramble about her Repute and what she's done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>What keeps you on the Pilgrimage?</b><br /> &quot;Not hope, really. Hope is a mistake.<br /> <br /> More like knowing the alternative. I've been off the road, and it fucking sucked. You imagine there's a point where things get so bad that they break and you magically push through into something different and better, but that point doesn't exist. You just keep being a monster. It never ends.<br /> <br /> Gotta keep pushing this stupid boulder, no matter how many times it rolls back down the hill. Sisyphus is in Hell, but at least he has a purpose.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Major or superlative Milestone: face an opportunity or invitation to give up hope and leave the Pilgrimage again (perhaps from Dead Girl) and choose what to do. It might also be totally unrelated to Dead Girl, I keep thinking it would be interesting to face some kind of weird Chronicles of Darkness third-way option that might seemingly let her escape the Pilgrimage and become something different and mysterious, taking a blind leap of Faith. &quot;Join your consciousness with the glowing sphere of light? Y/N&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>What would you give up to become human?</b><br /> &quot;My memories. My footprint. My past. Heartsblood. Dead Girl. All of it, the good and the bad. I don't want the stories other monsters tell about me, or the nightmares, or the memories of what I've done and stolen and killed. I want none of this to have ever happened, and I want a blank slate.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's cowardly. But I know I'm not strong enough to face the wreckage. The people I left behind have to sift meaning out of what I did, and I can't help them with that. I can't make this better. The most I can do is run away and hope if I become human, I'll never have existed at all.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Minor milestone ideas: learn that some Redeemed former Prometheans apparently lose their memories. Face a bad situation that Earth-Dies-Screaming created. Draw trouble to the throng because of something she did. Encounter a <i>sublimatus</i> she knew or knew of her. Fight someone she victimized who wants revenge, or just answers. Help fix a problem that Earth-Dies-Screaming caused. Be denied forgiveness by someone she hurt. Superlative milestone idea: face a situation where she can either concretely take responsibility for what she did as a Centimanus, or reaffirm that Earth-Dies-Screaming isn't her and she's become someone new and different.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> General ideas: I'm thinking Earth doesn't have a lot of experience socializing with humans, so basic stuff like &quot;make someone laugh&quot; or &quot;hold down a job&quot; or &quot;attend a place of worship&quot; or &quot;deal with anger constructively&quot; would be good.<br /> <br /> I don't know whether these necessarily count as Milestones, but I want to do stuff involving Promethean culture too, especially while following Lead. Talking to a weird Cuprum ascetic sage in the wilderness or the middle of the city. Meeting another Centimanus who returned to the Pilgrimage, or being told that all &quot;former&quot; Centimanus eventually relapse, or convincing a Freak to return.<br /> <br /> Definitely gotta do something involving Dead Girl, learning what's become of her, and coming to terms with that. Probably a few minor Milestones can be mined from this apart from a big confrontation, like visiting a place they were together, encountering something that traumatizes her (maybe she's extremely uncomfortable around other Galateids now or violently lashes out against the possibility of being in command of something), talking to a human who is/was in an abusive relationship, seeing a healthy relationship and understanding how they're different from what she had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some things that would definitely surprise her: organized and complex supernatural phenomena. Things that appear unnatural, but actually have a rational (if strange) explanation. Human-like societies of multiple intelligent supernatural beings parallel to human civilization, not just rogue bestial vampires and weird loners with a ghost inside them. Supernatural things that are beautiful in some way. </div> </div> </div>Encountering any of these things.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> All of those are just ideas and things I was thinking about- ultimately deciding Milestones is up to you of course!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T19:41:38-07:00","id":998573,"title":"","content":"Oh, Promethean culture will be a thing. I've liked the idea of this disparate, but relatively tight knit, community around the world. I'm not running with the assumption of &quot;only 100 Prometheans&quot; and instead running with &quot;Prometheans are one in a million&quot;, meaning the PCs <i>aren't </i>a serious percentage of Created population. We'll start intimate, and eventually get big, globe-trotting, and cosmic, but keeping that intense intimacy running through it all- as a good story about alchemy should.<br /> <br /> All of these things are great for Milestones! But I think the important thing to remember is that, for a lot of them, they'll be about choice and interpretation. I/The Principle can present the Milestone, but only you/Earth can decide what it means and take action. The only bad choice on a Milestone is walking away from it altogether. What Refinements do you want to see Earth <i>absolutely </i>practicing? What lessons are totally essential to her journey?<br /> <br /> Lastly, Earth is currently a Vigilante, so what is she fighting <i>for</i>? What's her cause?<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> As a side note, pertaining to the current scene, Earth will gain a Beat, and will also gain the &quot;Tainted Clue&quot; Condition. She can resolve it by apply a -2 penalty to a roll at some point in the future pertaining to the local Created and their experiences. Is that acceptable <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:37:21-07:00","id":998610,"title":"","content":"That Condition is fine if you want, you're the ST! Are you meaning to use the Tainted Clue tag from the Investigation system in the CofD core book? Because that's something a little different, although it would also fit here if you want to do this as a mini-Investigation with Clues and everything, that sounds fun. If we did that: maybe 2 or 3 Clues total to find an interesting and informative Pilgrim Mark or otherwise learn some occult insight?<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of negative Conditions usually have a little more bite than that. The ones you can get by charging an Alembic without showing Disfigurements are a great model for what to apply on a dramatic fail. Like the Alienated condition on 306 is a bit harsher and would be good here instead, gotta earn that d-fail Beat after all.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I slightly misread the Milestone suggestions on 298. Making a choice is always the important part, although some minors grant 1 Beat just for experiencing something.<br /> <br /> Earth should absolutely hit Plumbum, Argentum, and Phosphorum. I'd be happy to have some wildcard Refinements in there chosen by you as well. Only thing I'd say is that right now, I don't <i>think </i>she'd have Ferrum as a required one considering that her creator built her for that and she wasn't any good at it. I can imagine her having really mixed feelings about Aes (and the Branded Throng idea in general) given that Dead Girl used to practice it, but that doesn't necessarily mean it's not on her list. It might, though.<br /> <br /> She isn't motivated by a complex cause yet exactly, but finding one would be a good milestone. Right now, in line with her understanding of community, she's trying to understand the Vigilante by hanging around a particular neighborhood/block and targeting the people who are clearly (to her) making trouble. Muggings and street crime and robberies and stuff- property crime seems really important to humans. She's also seen evidence of abusers and domestic violence, but it confuses her, especially when the abuser is part of the community and the abused claim it's not a problem. She doesn't know whether that counts as a crime yet.<br /> <br /> As she understands it, Vigilantes answer trouble that comes from <i>within</i> as a means of community self-purging, but she'll probably learn to deal with the idea of outside threats as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-05-2016, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T03:29:15-07:00","id":998675,"title":"","content":"Awesome, things are taking off!<br /> Mark 5 will definately join up with Earth, but the Elysium Social Club is in the back of his mind already. Outside of clubs, people get robbed or beaten up, a perfect place to set an example. And maybe, just maybe, he will get to fight more than a human.<br /> <br /> Regarding Challenges/Milestones:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What Sort of Human do you want to be? Someone who's liked, even looked up to. </div> </div> </div>Being treated extremely badly because someone considers him beneath them; someone doing him a favour out of respect; someone following up on his Vigilante lifestyle because he looks up to his &quot;hero&quot; (which, of course, could end very badly- I also think this could be a major reason to switch to or even complete the Exemplar role); make a scene and get entirely ignored;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How have Humans taught you to fear and hate? By driving me away and even attacking me when all I do is help them. </div> </div> </div>Meet other people who have been driven from their rightful homes; Talk to puplic-service-people who get treated poorly despite of their work (hell, could be even a retail guy complaining about how he's being treated); Get invited into someone's home; receive help from someone despite having been a hassle; Experience how humans seek the comfort of other humans in dire times<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How did you split with your creator? Was suddenly left alone, without a word. Despite all the help before the departure, that left a bitter taste. </div> </div> </div>Meeting up with Mudbreaker would probably be a major Milestone I guess; Mark 5 WILL both punch and hug her (he only knows for sure about the former, though). Helping him resolve those needs might lead to coming to terms with the fact that things aren't always clear-cut. It would also depend on how Mudbreaker would react to her progeny and his lifestyle - and company.<br /> Meeting another Mark # would also be a minor or major Milestone, depending on their interaction and exchanges. The answers to any of these questions could count, too: Did Mudbreaker lose some or even destroy some of his progeny ? Were the others abandoned, too, or did they leave on their own? Did he achieve his goal with any of them? Why did he make Mark 5 so resilient? Has he, by now, fulfilled the Multiplicatio Milestone?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What keeps you on the Pilgrimage? Loneliness and dedication. </div> </div> </div>Experience and express happiness or other positive emotions about having a team/partner; be forsaken (imagined or not, justifieably due to other circumstances or not, doesn't matter) and left to fend for himself; overcome a problem/threat through repeated attempts and hard work; be in a situation where he enjoys being alone and contemplating; SEEK loneliness<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would you give up to become Human? My Name. </div> </div> </div>Learn about Redeemed who have lost their memory upon completing the Great Work; MAKE a Name for himself (through deeds and Repute).<br /> <br /> Mark 5 has generally a few problems/misconceptions that might need adressing<br /> - He only sees physical violence (or the threat thereof) as harmful: that people could be put under pressure from things other than physical threats, and that there is a difference between a construction worker (just fired because he disagrees of his bosses scumbag son dating his daughter) lashing out at his boss and a thug mugging someone for their possession is something he still has to learn. He might even mistake a bouncer kicking out an aggressive drunk for a situation where he has to &quot;intervene&quot;.<br /> He also thinks things are pretty much black-and-white: only good will come of good things (potential hardships, maybe, but in the end the result will be undeniably good). Intentions do not count for anything, unless it's a work in progress (someone weak training will of course take time to become strong).<br /> That's one of the reasons he is interested in following Earth around: Obviously having been evil, she expressed a desire to become good. How unusual.<br /> <br /> I'd like Mark 5 find a job, so he spends less time alone/among the homeless and learns more about social life. I'd like some punishment he handed out to come back to bite his ass or haunt him. Figure out that there are other ways to solve a situation than &quot;Beat up the wrong party as punishment&quot;, especially since that is not always what the victim of the conflict wishes for. Being left powerless in a situation, or forced with a situation he cannot overcome by himself, would be interesting, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> In regards to Refinements:<br /> I would absolutely love to see Cobalus, Mercurius and Plumbum (in any order, but I like the transition of Perfecting the body -&gt; Imperfections -&gt; Self-discovery-&gt; Source), and I wouldn't mind any wildcards chosen by you =D I don't really see Cuprum working at the moment, except maybe in combination with seeking loneliness, but that can change.<br /> <br /> In regards to his current Role (Soldier):<br /> Mark 5 wants to make the city safer. Taking out any sort of bigger threat would do the trick. Realizing his attempts to help created chaos could do the trick (and possibly make him turn away from Ferrum). Realizing he can only affect change on a smaller scale (one human life at a time), but that this is also a huge deal (means the world to that one human, after all), would be a nice lesson, too. Getting forced into a Diabolic Choice scenario like Tobey Maguire's Spiderman could teach a valuable lesson, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Ideas regarding Mark # 11-05-2016, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:19:59-07:00","id":998719,"title":"","content":"I have a character idea: a Promethean created by a woman to be the perfect boyfriend: somebody who was always there for her, who would be willing to cater to her sexual tastes. Basically, the ultimate doormat/submissive. Problem is, she started getting... clingy. What freedoms he had started getting revoked as she came to fear that other people wanted him for themselves. Tentatively, I'm naming him Adonis. <br /> <br /> Stuck on Refinements and Roles. Adonis is basically a big goofball. Not the most aware person, but he's sweet and he just likes people. He wants to understand human emotions better, and how humans are supposed to connect with each other. Whether he's doing it himself or helping somebody else to do it, he likes making people happy. Just looking over the Refinements, Aurum, Aes, and Phosphorum seem appropriate. Cuprum may work, too, if he ever feels that he needs to distance himself from people to progress on his Pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:25:02-07:00","id":998720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=998719#post998719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a character idea: a Promethean created by a woman to be the perfect boyfriend: somebody who was always there for her, who would be willing to cater to her sexual tastes. Basically, the ultimate doormat/submissive. Problem is, she started getting... clingy. What freedoms he had started getting revoked as she came to fear that other people wanted him for themselves. Tentatively, I'm naming him Adonis.<br /> <br /> Stuck on Refinements and Roles. Adonis is basically a big goofball. Not the most aware person, but he's sweet and he just likes people. He wants to understand human emotions better, and how humans are supposed to connect with each other. Whether he's doing it himself or helping somebody else to do it, he likes making people happy. Just looking over the Refinements, Aurum, Aes, and Phosphorum seem appropriate. Cuprum may work, too, if he ever feels that he needs to distance himself from people to progress on his Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! Adonis sounds like some high-presence Aurum Galateid to me, which would be interesting especially in regards to Earth's... issues with Galateids =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:30:05-07:00","id":998724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=998720#post998720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool! Adonis sounds like some high-presence Aurum Galateid to me, which would be interesting especially in regards to Earth's... issues with Galateids =D</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, my character and Caladriu's butting heads a little. Sounds familiar! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll try to whip up a character sheet this weekend and hopefully have that submitted by the end of the day tomorrow or Monday morning.<br /> <br /> Is this a &quot;ground-level&quot; Chronicle, or are the characters starting out with some extra Experiences?<br /> <br /> Just sat down to do the sheet and initially put down his concept as &quot;Goofy Prince Charming,&quot; but my attribute spread made me realize that Adonis is basically Rocky from RHPS. So &quot;Real-life Rocky Horror&quot; it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 11-05-2016, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:06:12-07:00","id":998741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=998724#post998724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, my character and Caladriu's butting heads a little. Sounds familiar! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll try to whip up a character sheet this weekend and hopefully have that submitted by the end of the day tomorrow or Monday morning.<br /> <br /> Is this a &quot;ground-level&quot; Chronicle, or are the characters starting out with some extra Experiences?<br /> <br /> Just sat down to do the sheet and initially put down his concept as &quot;Goofy Prince Charming,&quot; but my attribute spread made me realize that Adonis is basically Rocky from RHPS. So &quot;Real-life Rocky Horror&quot; it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>10 xp, distributed among normal and vitriolic however you want.<br /> <br /> Never seen that one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:15:53-07:00","id":998748,"title":"","content":"You also start at Pilgrimage 2 and with a completed Role. Which Refinement will Adonis start on (It needs to be a Basic Refinement), what Role have you completed, and what Alembics do you currently possess?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Alienated does fit better. I'll amend the post.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> I think it's worth mentioning that the Alternate Identity Merit is meant to represent a mortal identity supported by documentation. You can be Rockbreaker the vigilante without needing to spend the dot on it, but having a mostly functional human identity would be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-05-2016, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:36:36-07:00","id":998755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=998748#post998748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> I think it's worth mentioning that the Alternate Identity Merit is meant to represent a mortal identity supported by documentation. You can be Rockbreaker the vigilante without needing to spend the dot on it, but having a mostly functional human identity would be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, makes sense. I'll change the sheet, so he'll have a basic identity as a certain Mark Stone (creativity, thy name is Wormwood). Should be enough to be able to get a job as a bouncer (in shady parts of the city), construction worker or similar jobs with low prestige / high physical demand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:12:54-07:00","id":998769,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> Never seen Rocky Horror Picture Show? It's a campy 70s musical that riffs on Frankenstein. A sexually depraved, cross-dressing mad scientist (played by Tim Curry) makes a creature to serve as his lover. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> He's on the Refinement of Aurum, and has completed the Role of Follower: he wanted to learn if humans really could be trusted, and so he got into another relationship with a woman who deliberately reminded him of his demiurge, as a submissive. All-in-all, it went rather well, and even though he has &quot;moved on&quot; from the relationship, he's actually made a friend. He's currently on the Role of Companion, trying to learn how to relate to humans on equal footing. Basically, he learned how relationships with unequal power exchange right, and is now working on equal power exchange. The Role of Leader will revolve around him conquering the role his demiurge and former dominant played for him. <br /> <br /> He's got Assimilation from Deception and Eros from Mesmerism: one to symbolically Follower, and the other to represent Companion. He'll probably Calcify both of those so that he can retain those as mementoes of his Pilgrimage so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:27:44-07:00","id":998778,"title":"","content":"Seems like a really nice progression. As a note, since you're on to a second Role in the same Refinement, you can pick up another Alembic in each Transmutation! If you choose to Clacify one or both of your first two Alembics, you'll have three in total.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T09:10:07-07:00","id":998789,"title":"","content":"Alright. He'll spend two of those extra Experiences to Calcify Assimilation from Deception as a souvenir of Follower. He has Stalker from Deception and Eros from Mesmerism for his current role of Companion. He'll pick up an extra dot of Azoth and three dots in skills. <br /> <br /> For Elpis, I'm thinking Love, since he was &quot;built&quot; for love and wants to understand it fully. For Torment, I'm thinking either Na\u00efve, to represent his misunderstanding of human nature and his occasional inability to realize that humans don't always want physical contact and sexual gratification all the time, and that not everybody wants it with him; or make a custom Jealous Torment, because part of me likes the idea that his demiurge created him to be 100% faithful, and it would be a nice &quot;become his own antithesis&quot; if he acts towards others like his demiurge acted towards him. <br /> <br /> I'll have to think about the questions for the Milestones. I have a tentative Merits list drawn up, I just need time to hammer out his backstory and how they fit together. I'm currently thinking that he's some sort of horrific amalgamation of body parts from soap opera actors that his demiurge had a crush on- his head comes from her absolute favorite, and she actually murdered him to get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:09:44-07:00","id":998996,"title":"","content":"Okay, I think I've got Adonis' write-up squared away. <div align=\"center\"><b>Appearance</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://67.media.tumblr.com/e587ea660922638273dc7c667afeb354/tumblr_mijmll9MPK1qh55b0o1_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Stats</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Name: Adonis<br /> Concept: Real-life Rocky Horror<br /> <br /> Lineage: Galateid<br /> Refinement: Aurum<br /> Role: Companion<br /> Mastered Roles: Follower<br /> <br /> Elpis: Love<br /> Torment: Jealous<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b><br /> Intelligence: 1<br /> Wits: 2<br /> Resolve: 3<br /> <br /> Strength: 3<br /> Dexterity: 2<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Presence: 3<br /> Manipulation: 3<br /> Composure: 2<br /> <br /> <b>Skills</b><br /> Crafts: 1<br /> Medicine (Aftercare): 2<br /> Occult: 1<br /> <br /> Athletics: 2<br /> Brawl: 2<br /> Larceny: 1<br /> Stealth: 1<br /> Survival: 2<br /> <br /> Empathy (Emotions): 3<br /> Expression: 3<br /> Persuasion (Seduction): 3<br /> Socialize: 2<br /> Streetwise: 1<br /> Subterfuge: 1<br /> <br /> Area of Expertise (Seduction): 1<br /> Famous Face: 1<br /> Hovel: 2<br /> Safe Place: 1<br /> Striking Looks: 2<br /> True Friend (Lily): 3<br /> True Friend (Erwin): 1<br /> Brute Force Style: 3<br /> <br /> Bestowment: Unearthly Mein<br /> Refinement Condition: Masked<br /> <br /> Transmutations: Deception, Mesmerism<br /> Alembics: Assimilation, Eris, Eros, Stalker<br /> Calcified Alembics: Eros<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Learn more about Mark Austin (long-term); bring down Amalgama; find a social group of humans to join<br /> <br /> Size: 5<br /> Health: 7<br /> Speed: 10<br /> Defense: 4<br /> Initiative Mod: 4<br /> <br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Azoth: 2<br /> Pyros: 5/10, 2 per round<br /> Pilgrimage: 2</div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>History</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Greeks, among whom the Galateids originated, were fond of cautionary tales. If Adonis could be said to be a cautionary tale, he's a warning against the dangers of obsessive celebrity crushes. His demiurge was a woman named Sharon, who had unhealthy fixation on a number of actors who had appeared in teen-marketed dramas and soap operas. She wanted to date them... but she couldn't settle on just one. When she found out that four of them were dead of various causes, a twisted idea crossed her mind: she would take some of their body parts and use them to build a man who was the sum of their best parts. Over the course of weeks, she &quot;collected&quot; the needed parts: arms from one, legs from another, torso from this one, manhood from that one. But she ran into a problem: the one she wanted the most, Mark Austin, was alive. She found where he lived- he had dropped out of the public eye and was living alone in solitude- and murdered him. And she took his head to complete her perfect man.<br /> <br /> Long she labored on her creation, until finally, his heart beat, and he took a shuddering breath. She named him &quot;Mark&quot; and set about teaching him that his purpose was to satisfy her. For a while, he did just that, diligently. He was the perfect boyfriend, catering to her every whim, and indulging her every fantasy. But Disquiet inevitably set in, and it manifested as irrational jealousy in Sharon. First, she told him to stop going outside, since she had noticed people giving Mark interested- or was it lustful?- looks. But then she started to fear that he wanted to leave her, so she started restricting his movement further and further: doors started getting locked, then he was locked in a single room until Sharon was ready to play with him, and then he was chained to the wall. The Disquiet culminated with Sharon thinking that Mark no longer loved her, and she decided to destroy him. Some heartfelt begging- and brute force- gained Mark a reprieve, and he fled.<br /> <br /> Mark, now going by Adonis, embarked on his Pilgrimage to see if the humans he so deeply envied were truly trust worthy. To accomplish this, he wandered to Winnipeg and took the Refinement of Aurum. He found a woman named Lily, who reminded him of Sharon. Lily was a domme, and Adonis became her submissive. It was a fragile thing, touch and go at times, but Lily slowly gained Adonis' trust. He gained a friend, and mastered a Role. While he is no longer formally dating Lily, they are still close, and occasionally meet for a session. Now, Adonis is working on the Role of Companion: he has learned how to play a lesser to humans, now he wants to learn how to relate to them as equals.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 07-20-2017, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:42:33-07:00","id":999045,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> good call on the idea of getting him the identity as Mark Stone.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> Adonis looks really fascinating, especially seeing as he's going to be recognizable to a decent subset of the population. What happened to his Demiurge? Did she manage to avoid criminal charges? How old is she? Would he ever want to see her again? Either way, I think Sharon is going to come up at some point. I have a <i>very </i>particular antagonist planned out for later in the Chronicle, and I think between Adonis and Earth's backstories, there's going to be a lot of material to build off of.<br /> <br /> Update is now up. Feel free to join in when you'd like, Haberdasher. Get a feel for the character on the fly, I doubt we're going to make much progress on the Pilgrimage right this instant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T04:53:15-08:00","id":999164,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> Thanks! Sharon is still around. I don't think she's been arrested: she snuck into some morgues, dug up a couple graves, and checked to make sure Mark Austin wouldn't be missed for a while at least. She's probably escaped criminal charges for the time being- this being the Chronicles of Darkness, it wouldn't surprise me if she manages to escape arrest for a good long while. She and Lily are both in the late 30s, blonde, similar facial features. Again, that's why he chose to get into contact with Lily. The possibility of meeting Sharon again... maybe further down the line, when he's getting close to the end of his Pilgrimage. Come back to the person who both created him and tried to destroy him, and show her how much he's grown in her absence, if for no other reason than to demonstrate to the both of them that he's moved on and is so far beyond her now. <br /> <br /> I realized that I forgot to answer his Milestone questions. As far as those go: <br /> <br /> <b>What sort of human do you want to be? </b>Adonis thinks he wants to be a caretaker of some sort. Maybe as a spouse and father, maybe as a living assistant. That, of course, kind of clashes with his very specific skill set. So he has an internal nature vs. nurture conflict going on. <br /> <br /> <b>How have humans taught you to fear and hate? </b>Adonis fears jealousy. Ironically, it's his Torment, but he'll never forget the look on Sharon's face as she came at him with the carving knife to dismember him. He also despises how humans often see each other as toys and means to an end- seeing somebody take advantage of another person, especially sexually, annoys the hell out of him. <br /> <br /> <b>How did you split from your creator? </b>Sharon wasn't exactly stable to begin with. Dismembering corpses and murdering an idol, and then using their body parts to create her own personal sex slave didn't do her any favors either. Disquiet did the rest. Nothing like attempted murder to make you want to get away from your demiurge. <br /> <br /> <b>What keeps you on your Pilgrimage? </b>Adonis wants to fully understand what love is, and what it entails: the patience, the compromise, the trust. He knows he was created for a very narrow and twisted definition of love, so he wants to understand it fully. <br /> <br /> <b>What would you give up to be human? </b>Right now, Adonis is willing to pay any price. But he's especially willing to give up his looks and charms, since part of him wonders if they are a hindrance on his Pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:13:32-08:00","id":999254,"title":"","content":"All really good stuff. Does Adonis already know Earth and Mark 5, or will this be the first time they meet? What do Adonis' Disfigurements look like? Where is his Hovel/Safe Place and what is it like?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> you still can choose a couple more Alembics. You get one in each Transmutation when starting a Refinement, and one more in each when you complete a Role. With Eros calcified, you should have three Mesmerism Alembics and two Deception Alembics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-06-2016, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:13:37-08:00","id":999389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=999254#post999254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All really good stuff. Does Adonis already know Earth and Mark 5, or will this be the first time they meet? What do Adonis' Disfigurements look like? Where is his Hovel/Safe Place and what is it like?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> you still can choose a couple more Alembics. You get one in each Transmutation when starting a Refinement, and one more in each when you complete a Role. With Eros calcified, you should have three Mesmerism Alembics and two Deception Alembics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay! In that case, he'll have Stalker from Deception, and Phobos from Mesmerism. <br /> <br /> Depending on how recently Earth came to Winnipeg, he may have heard of them but not have met them in person. He'll probably be wary of them if he knows they're a former Centimanus. He's probably met Mark 5 before, and certainly knows of him. That Earth and Mark 5 know each other will be a surprise. <br /> <br /> His Disfigurements are the typical &quot;stitched-together&quot; thing. His sources all had slightly different skin tones, so his limbs, body, and head are all noticeably different colors, and the places where Sharon stitched the pieces together are painfully obvious if bare skin shows. In most cases, the difference between his hands, and the stitches around his neck, will tip people off. <br /> <br /> His Hovel is an out-of-the-way room in a tenement building. Nobody is using it, and nobody cares that he comes and goes. Anybody asks, he could just turn on the charm. The building he sleeps in is pretty noisy all hours of the day. He just lets the noise wash over him each night as he falls asleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:14:21-08:00","id":999392,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't be a superhero story without the protagonists fighting when they first meet!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> I don't think that's quite how calcifying works, unless I misread page 118. Adonis would have 2 Alembics from each Transmutation, but he can keep the ones he calcified when he switches to a different Refinement.<br /> <br /> I haven't really decided if Earth uses she/her or they/their. Both would be fitting, but everyone Earth knows has used &quot;she&quot; so far. Let's go with she/her, but it's something I'm interested in coming back to in-character! Monsterhearts has me in the mood to think about that in a supernatural setting, haha.<br /> <br /> e: Earth has been in Winnipeg for like 2-3 weeks, and came here after the events in Powerview-Pine Falls. She does have a Repute that precedes her, but it would also be neat to meet someone with no preconceptions about her. I'll leave it up to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> if Adonis knows of her or not, either is okay by me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-06-2016, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:59:56-08:00","id":999446,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> He's probably had enough time to heard about her, then. Her reputation precedes her. Hasn't met her, and it's certainly a rocky introduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:06:45-08:00","id":999451,"title":"","content":"I was secretly hoping you'd dramatic fail that roll too and we'd start off on a wild goose chase for a completely nonexistent threat. Get all Foucault's Pendulum with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:04:12-08:00","id":999475,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I expected to get a Dramatic Failure on that one. But nope, not only did I get a success, I got a 10. Which I know doesn't technically affect anything, but it's still amusing as hell. The two Tammuz see a message for Earth to get out of Winnipeg, and the poor Galateid is standing there all, &quot;Um, guys, it's just graffiti, you're reading way too far into this.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T21:06:40-08:00","id":999562,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> the example given mentions that the Promethean in question, Chicago, Calcified three Alembics after mastering Stannum before moving on to Plumbum. She keeps all three of those Alembics, and immediately expresses the fourth since when you're practicing a Role you need to express an Alembic. My understanding was that Calcifying an Alembic fixes it in your alchemical makeup and not only allows you to keep it, but also allows you to expand your repertoire. Reasonably certain that Matt posted something in the forums that supports that reading, but I'm away from my laptop at the moment and thus cannot find it to back myself up.<br /> <br /> Secondly, duly noted on Earth going by 'she'. I remembered some of the Milestones and decided to go with the neutral 'they' to test it out. I'm guessing we'll return to the pronoun tango at some point once Earth gets over enough self-loathing to be a little bit more introspective.<br /> <br /> All that said, I find it hilarious that the dice have the occasional sense of humour. Adonis sees the graffiti for what it is, but Earth is adamant. I'm interested to see where it will be going from here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T21:16:16-08:00","id":999563,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> where would Mark have met Adonis? Did he see him in action? I'd go with Mark 5 having helped him when he got harrassed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Btw, he totally believes Adonis is from Arizona now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:09:07-08:00","id":999749,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a>, the update is posted Roll Wits + Empathy to determine the honesty and emotional state of the other Created. If <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> want, you guys can fail the roll to resolve the Alienated Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:14:30-08:00","id":999752,"title":"","content":"I already failed the chance die roll ^^&quot; Will resolve it sometime later. This is getting heated xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T10:38:21-08:00","id":999808,"title":"","content":"And the escalation continues! Did I mention Market Square is like two blocks away from police headquarters? Because it's like two blocks away from police headquarters.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I found the post from Developer Matt that backs up my reading <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations/page3\">here</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=902684#post902684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, sure. You can calcify any time you have the XP to do it, which then opens up another slot in the Transmutation for you.<br /> <br /> The second question...hmm. I actually don't think we address that. I would allow a player to do that, sure, though it'd probably require a scene and some cool roleplaying just to explain the character's though process.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T10:43:25-08:00","id":999810,"title":"","content":"OH SHII---<br /> <br /> This is going on Worldstar in a minute. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> the gauntlet again falls on you to resolve a spat before it turns into a big dumb brawl.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> That does kinda make more sense, you should immediately get something for spending XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:20:45-08:00","id":999828,"title":"","content":"Well, let's hope he doesn't fail his roll, otherwise ST will have to save us xD<br /> Seriously though, such drama such early into the game =D<br /> I do hope this chills, but since I still gotta resolve my Alienated.... &gt;=D<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","na