th.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:38:24-08:00","id":1026543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1025610#post1025610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haha, well Adonis needs the company. Sanguine and Choleric are diametrically opposed, maybe Phlegm can split the difference. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, I'm hoping Adonis will be a positive influence on introspective Scout. Him finding Regret as a fellow originist will certainly be interesting, though I have a feeling they are coming at the same Transmutation from fairly different angles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:24:20-08:00","id":1026592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1026543#post1026543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah, I'm hoping Adonis will be a positive influence on introspective Scout. Him finding Regret as a fellow originist will certainly be interesting, though I have a feeling they are coming at the same Transmutation from fairly different angles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it might come down to more of an age thing. Regret is still very young in the Saturnine Night, so he's still trying to understand the ins-n-outs of his condition. Hence the Originist angle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T13:17:38-08:00","id":1026664,"title":"","content":"Will Adonis have to bow out to keep his date with Erwin tonight, or can he stay to complete the scene with the others and still have time for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T20:50:21-08:00","id":1026840,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> Adonis definitely has time to stay and finish the scene with the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T00:59:40-08:00","id":1026907,"title":"","content":"I think I probably hit the &quot;meet someone who knows me through Repute&quot; Aspiration, or will before the scene is over. Also realized I could've added Repute to that Expression roll, not that it would have made a difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:26:21-08:00","id":1026953,"title":"","content":"Oh ma gosh, I actually got what I think was a pretty decent first Ramble. ^_^<br /> <br /> Thanks again everyone for still letting me join the game, this is by far one of the weirdest character's I've made and I love it! Also, Wormwood I think a budding frienemiship is in store for our two characters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T05:30:05-08:00","id":1026976,"title":"","content":"Indeed, there is quite some potential for some infighting =D<br /> <br /> <br /> Also: Loving the plothooks! Hope Scout decides to go after the Vampires, Mark 5 would love putting one or two of the things down.<br /> Werewolves are scary, though. Crazy Moon spirit doesn't sound good, either.<br /> But: Following Mudbreaker sounds awesome!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T07:54:58-08:00","id":1027026,"title":"","content":"And there is Scout's piece of the Ramble. Complete with tiny tinny squeaky voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T18:13:40-08:00","id":1027370,"title":"","content":"Mark 5 is getting a lesson in ethics and morality at this Ramble. This is why having a Mimic around is useful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T00:25:54-08:00","id":1027482,"title":"","content":"Poor Mark 5 is all Insecure now. Everyone so hung up on a concept he doesnt get =D<br /> Also, this whole Ramble seems intent on tackling his Intention-milestone, which is fine by me :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T21:31:12-08:00","id":1028426,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> the update is up! I'm not really sure what's left to handle with the Ramble. You've been introduced to several potential plot hooks (and you have the existing Amalgama LTD plot thread to pursue), you've been introduced to two new characters, and all in all I think the scene got done what it needed to get done. All that's really left to do is for Scout and Regret to attach themselves to the Throng, and for the Throng to decide what to do next.<br /> <br /> Minus Adonis, of course, he's got plans, but the rest of you can decide what you're going to do for the rest of the night.<br /> <br /> I was also wondering if I could get some feedback about the Ramble and what you guys thought. What did you like, what did you feel was missing, did it <i>feel </i>like a Promethean thing? The books really have no guideline for how to handle more than a handful of Created at a time, and a larger group trying to form a community is kind of unprecedented. The Created have a tendency to feel like the kicked dogs of the Chronicles of Darkness, they have it pretty rough, and it would be easy to make every Promethean's life a long slog of one tragedy after another constantly chasing after the hope of the New Dawn, but I figured I would try and show some Created who have their lives a little more together, who are hopeful and determined and vivacious. Promethean can feel pretty dreary, sometimes, but I didn't want all the hope and beauty to come from humans, I wanted some of it to come from the Created themselves, and I hope that came across.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T00:44:29-08:00","id":1028456,"title":"","content":"I think you succeeded in that task beautifully. I certainly felt that it was a truly Promethean gathering, and the stories told for the aesthetic and tone very well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I do have a side question though, the group is a Throng but are they a Branded Throng? Because <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> and myself could make us all a Branded Throng since we both have the proper Alembic. That might be the best way to stick the party together, because it looks like Regret and Scout both have eyes on studying Earth and Mark 5's Throng. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T03:24:06-08:00","id":1028479,"title":"","content":"Alright, there's the long-delayed fleshing out! And it sets the tone for any Branding that might happen soon. I'm down with forming a branded throng but Earth might need some convincing to join it. Earth and Mark 5 would have slightly reduced benefits with two Tammuz in the throng, but it would still be a benefit.<br /> <br /> If the non-Adonis members of the throng want to do something next, scoping out those infested tunnels under the Exchange sounds fun. Or if people want to do solo or duo stuff, that would be good too. &quot;Getting to know each other one on one against an action-y backdrop,&quot; like Earth and Mark 5 have been doing, would be a good next scene.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> I'd like to talk to Satin for just a little bit longer, like 1 more post before rejoining the other PCs, but otherwise I'm okay with ending the scene.<br /> <br /> I strongly enjoyed the Ramble, I meant to post that earlier. The location is great and grounds us in Winnipeg, we learned something new and interesting about the setting, and the way you write a bunch of background characters swapping stories and opinions used the crowd scene very well without overshadowing the PCs. It's great that it gave everyone a chance to introduce themselves in-character, this is a very organic way to meet Scout and Regret and give them the spotlight. This was probably my favorite scene in the game so far. I would enjoy more scenes where we can bicker and hang around with NPCs, you write them well and it lends itself well to a text medium. [any chance of a minor Milestone for everyone addressing a Ramble for the first time?]<br /> <br /> I agree that it's good to have Prometheans as more vivacious and active and hopeful and community-oriented, that's more fun to deal with than drudgery and misery. They're outsiders, but they have each other, potentially. On that note: Satin is really cool and I'd like to see more of them, especially since we have no Ulgan PCs and they might be a path to some Milestones for Earth. I'm officially signaling that I'm Interested In This NPC!<br /> <br /> At first I thought it was a little implausible that there would be a large-ish gathering in a prominent location on a weekly basis, but it works. Maybe Winnipeg is known in Canada for its unusually large and connected Ramble, and there's a Sentry or two who works on keeping humans uninterested. I like that there's no formal rituals or titles or anything, it's just a kind of cobbled-together swap meet and hangout in a vaguely meaningful setting. I was surprised there was no Wasteland since that's presented as a big hurdle to Prometheans forming stable communities, but that can be explained away. There's an adventure in the 1E sourcebook Pandora's Book (I think) that centers on a semi-permanent Promethean community in post-Katrina New Orleans, which of course ends horribly because of Wasteland and Firestorms and not everyone having good intentions, but 1E had different setting assumptions and it doesn't need to end that way everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T05:44:41-08:00","id":1028514,"title":"","content":"I can only support what was already said: awesome scene! I liked the tone a lot, and as I already said, the setting was very well chosen. I wouldn't mind more of that happening at all!<br /> <br /> In regards to what to do next: If asked, Mark 5 will gladly help clean those vampire-infested tunnels, but other than that he would really, really like to go look for Mudbreaker and might even try to steer everyone in that direction. If they don't agree and go for Amalgama, he will be forced to chose between his desire (meeting Mudbreaker) and his mission (Earth), which would be cool of and in itself! =D<br /> So far, I'd like to play out the &quot;There is no black&amp;white!&quot; part and maybe achieve Mark5's first Milestone with that.<br /> <br /> Btw, Earth really has become some sort of central piece to the throng xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T07:16:19-08:00","id":1028534,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed the Ramble. Thought it was excellent. Scout has sooo many things to write now. And I have to go remember what his genitor was named.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T19:08:27-08:00","id":1029419,"title":"","content":"Thank-you for all the great feedback guys! I'm glad you're enjoying yourselves. I think I can stretch the Ramble out a post or two more, because as always, your characters are providing some really engaging interactions. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> the way you wrote Mark 5's thought process is definitely worth a Milestone and a couple of Vitriol Beats.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> is there anything you guys wanted to cover before the Ramble ends?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T20:35:04-08:00","id":1029451,"title":"","content":"I wrote a post but it got deleted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Basically: I'd like to leave the Ramble with a bit of seemingly-irrelevant information or a status update like &quot;the Pilgrimage of Highwinds, genitor of Scout, has ended&quot; that we can pass on to new people we meet in the future. It would be cool to be a link in a long chain that may or may not find the right person eventually. I figure some people will similarly spread the word that Earth is looking for Dead Girl on their travels, even if they don't know either individual, so that information is floating freely out there in the world now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1028514#post1028514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, Earth really has become some sort of central piece to the throng xD</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kinda cool! That Repute 2 really pays for itself. As long as I'm not overshadowing anybody, I like that her reputation is a beacon that drew a random collection of pilgrims together from across the wastes. It feels like a really natural way for the throng to form and stick together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T22:39:57-08:00","id":1029479,"title":"","content":"I think I'm good with the Ramble coming to a close. Regret in his own way has tried to offer to initiate a Branded Throng in his own way, but just doesn't have the right words for it. I think Scout might need to pick up the difference. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, excellent posts everyone. This is everything I ever wanted out of a Promethean game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T12:46:23-08:00","id":1029710,"title":"","content":"So Mark 5 is convinced Regret is somehow informed through the Principle and send to help with the mission of Earth, too, and is starting to wonder what the hell is going to come after them if the Principle throws so many helpers at them.<br /> Regret'd need the rest of the throng's permission, since Mark 5 doesn't feel he has any authority to decide for them, but I have a feeling Adonis is going to welcome him^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:17:24-08:00","id":1029751,"title":"","content":"The best part too is that Regret has no idea what Mark 5's mission is, Regret in his ignorant youth calls the Pilgrimage the Mission since that's what his residual memories reinforce. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:59:55-08:00","id":1029777,"title":"","content":"I don't mean to be a bug, but I'm having trouble following the conversations without text colors, especially when its three or more of us talking to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:11:23-08:00","id":1029785,"title":"","content":"Yeah, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> do you want to pick colors for your spoken text? We've been kinda inconsistent but <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Earth</span> and <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Adonis</span> and <span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span> have them. They're pretty easy to add if you're not posting on mobile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:13:53-08:00","id":1029788,"title":"","content":"Sorry <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a>, I don't have access to a computer atm so I've had to use just my smart phone. The problem is I don't know how to change the color of the text so I've been having everything Regret says be text message style while everything he thinks is written in paragraphs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T00:45:03-08:00","id":1029953,"title":"","content":"Having to rely on my smart phone AT times is the reason for my inconsistencies, too.<br /> If you can color code there, I dont know how.<br /> We could use regret ' s example and at least put the Name of the speaker infront of the Text when we cant use color.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T11:25:34-08:00","id":1030150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1029777#post1029777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean to be a bug, but I'm having trouble following the conversations without text colors, especially when its three or more of us talking to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're fine <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a>. I usually just don't do that because I'm colorblind. Not like, monochrome, but a severe deutan, which gives me a hard time deciphering several closer colors, especially like what Earth and Adonis use. I'll pick something if it helps though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Added color to Scout's previous spoken text. I hope that blue is different enough from Mark 5's","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 01-11-2017, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:09:09-08:00","id":1030327,"title":"","content":"Yeah, apparently mobile devices don't let you access the text-editing tools. I'll try to keep that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a>, and try to write my posts so that I mention who's saying what. And yes, your blue is a bright blue, whereas Mark 5's is a dark blue. The contrast is pretty obvious, at least to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T02:55:35-08:00","id":1030490,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> Something I was thinking as this scene wraps up: would you like us to be more proactive in saying what we want to pursue next? I feel like we've sometimes been waiting on you to toss us the next thing to do, and I don't know whether that's your preferred style as an ST. It's a lot of fun for me to be tossed into situations of your design and work them out, but you might find it easier to be reactive to us instigating stuff. Or maybe not! I don't know.<br /> <br /> Here's some stuff on my mind for what happens next:<ul><li>I'm down with starting a branded throng, maybe even before we leave the Ramble. I was imagining Earth being hesitant and reluctant and putting it off at first, but the more I think about it, there's no reason not to just make the bond and get the mechanical effects and see what trouble that gets us into, rather than waiting at the threshold.</li> <li>Making my intentions with Satin a little more clear: I want her to realize Satin isn't a she/her/lady/chick and have her awkward advances rebuffed, learn something about gender and identity from a Promethean perspective (doesn't need to be an onscreen conversation) that she can then practice on her own, and then have them as a future contact. I don't particularly want to play out any kind of romance/dating story, but I maybe want to establish &quot;Earth is very interested in Satin but bad at expressing it because of her awful experiences with Dead Girl&quot; as something happening offscreen in the background. Earth needs to work on herself before she gets involved with anybody, yo.</li> <li>I really want to help Mark 5 follow Mudbreaker up north, but I might want to do a little bit more in Winnipeg with the new kids before we leave. Pursuing the Vigilante Role further would be good. I've been thinking about what her personal code is, and one option is &quot;people who feed on others need to be punished&quot; in line with the Amalgama LTD situation. That could also open up to things like humans who leech off of others, abusers who drain their victims, etc. I'd like to broaden her horizon a little and draw a connection between a Promethean-specific thing like lacuna and stealing Vitriol, and a more human situation like eroding the self-worth of another person.</li> <li>A different facet of her Vigilante code could be a specific grudge against creators who don't take responsibility for their progeny. That's a really personal issue for her and one that would be easy to tie in to helping Mark 5 find Mudbreaker. I'd like Earth to give some (awful) advice to others about their problems, not only be the focus of others' attention. And it could lead to some introspection about owning what she did as Earth-Dies-Screaming, and taking responsibility for the metaphorical and literal monsters she let out of Pandora's Box.</li> <li>Venturing into the catacombs to fight Unborn and get cool treasure sounds fun, Earth is definitely built for that kind of gameplay. A simple dungeon crawl with a randomly generated little map can be fun, I did that in the Mage game I run and my players really enjoyed it as a change of pace. But if other people think that would be a drag or their character isn't suited to it, it's not necessary. I don't want to drag everyone into an initiative-based combat scene that we're not interested in (although that does interest me, for what it's worth.)</li> <li>If we were going to pursue Amalagama further, Earth isn't super well-suited to social and investigative situations, although she does have a lot of Intimidation and a smattering of other Social skills that could help with making people talk. I'm open to doing that next, it's just that someone else would need to take the lead, which is fine by me.</li> <li>I would like to trigger an Elpis Vision via the Elpis Aspiration (&quot;witness a sincere expression of faith&quot;) to get an idea of what completing her Role will look like. This could happen during the current scene, or by a visit to the burned-out cathedral, or something.</li> <li>Once she resolves Disconnected somehow and gets over her current aversion to humans, I want Earth to spend some more time at the community garden. It doesn't need to a big onscreen thing except for the occasional short vignette, I just want to establish that this is a place where she's occasionally laboring and being exposed to humans. Until Disquiet sets in, of course.</li> <li>After Vigilante is finished, Earth is probably going to go Cuprum because she wants to reshape her body with Metamorphosis in a non-Flux way. Like, her in-character justification is that she wants the alchemy powers, she'll try whatever Role she hears about whether it's on her Pilgrimage or not. I don't think you need a mentor for a basic Refinement, you can just kinda reflect on it for a while and switch. However it works out, it would be nice to be on Cuprum by the time we're tracking Mudbreaker in the wilderness.</li> <li>Most of my Experience expenditures for a while are probably going to be Merits, because Promethean 2E has a lot of really cool 1-dot stuff and I want all of it. Buying up Vivid Dreams and growing increasingly in touch with the Principle seems like a good goal.</li> <li>Finally, at some point I want Earth to get <i>real drunk</i> with Adonis, go to a club in Winnipeg, attempt to dance with humans, demand that the DJ play <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-pgJByML5xY\" target=\"_blank\">sappy songs</a> so she can cry about her ex and make a huge ugly Disquieted mess.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> I'll pick new Aspirations once we start a new Chapter, I think that's how it works. Unless you want me to pick them now. Are we at or near a Chapter break now that the gang's all here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T09:27:13-08:00","id":1030619,"title":"","content":"Totally down with going after mudbreaker or some dungeon-crawling!<br /> For Mark 5, getting to know the New guys and branding their throng would be cool (never alone, even when not with the others!), and I'd like him to go about his vigilante work in a new Form (hello, season 2 arrow!). <br /> I would like to explore the 'not-being-appreciated'- concept that came up in his reasoning to accepted regret, and observe the others hit on somebody like Earth is doing now. It will confuse him to no end! :-)<br /> His role is not fulfilled yet (actually, at which point is it?) And i do not See him change any time soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T12:41:09-08:00","id":1030730,"title":"","content":"Sounds fantastic to me too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly Regret will be happy so long as he's there to witness these amazing moments in the other Promethean's Pilgrimage. <br /> <br /> The only plot point of his own that would be cool to explore later would be to introduce his Genitor Prime into the story. I see her as an antagonist who's abandoned the Pilgrimage to become human, but not to become something other than a Promethean. In my head she would be on the Refinement of Argentum and studying other Supernatural creatures when she hit the revelation: &quot;Hey, why be a frail human when I could be one of these specimens?&quot; Prime is supposed to represent someone who hits a dead end in the Pilgrimage but is too proud to go back so instead they try to smash a path through the wall without resorting to Flux. She would have nothing but distain for Flux.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T13:47:15-08:00","id":1030764,"title":"","content":"I think Adonis wants to focus on wrapping up the Amalgama LTD plot, since he has the highest personal stakes in it (i.e., Erwin). A dungeon crawl could be fun, but I'm thinking that might have to wait until Adonis picks up a Refinement that gives him more combat-oriented Alembics- or I could play him like a D&amp;D rogue and try to do some stealth-ing and backstabbing. <br /> <br /> Heading out of the city and up north could be a nice change of pace. But again, I don't think Adonis is quite ready. Maybe if he gets more introspective or decides he needs to separate himself from humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T15:06:40-08:00","id":1030817,"title":"","content":"Scout is generally interested in three things right now:<br /> 1) Seeing what Earth (and the others) do with their pilgrimage as a way to study them.<br /> 2) Find ALL the Athanors!<br /> 3) Learn about Fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:15:32-08:00","id":1031192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1030490#post1030490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> Snipped for brevity</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank-you for all of that detail, I like knowing what my players want to do at some point in the campaign, and especially insights into the character. Generally, I like it to be half and half. There are stories I want to tell, but ultimately they're your characters. My most pressing concern will be to finish up the Ramble, sort a few final things out with Satin, and deal with the Amalgama LTD plot, which will likely be the focus of the next Chapter. Within the next post or two, we'll wrap the scene, wrap the chapter, and have a bit of time skip. This will give you guys time to do some Extended Actions and flesh out your characters' everyday lives.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> we will absolutely be able to incorporate her Elpis Aspiration and trigger an Elpis Vision, and then get her to finish the Vigilante Role. Her owning up to her past actions as Earth-Dies-Screaming would be a good thing to have happen. I also like drawing parallels between Promethean and Human things, since Alchemy is Allegory anyways. I also think that Earth will get an opportunity to enjoy mastery of the Vigilante, at least for a little while. When you master a Role, you <i>no longer cause Disquiet or Wastelands</i>. Give her some peace. Also, to answer earlier questions, it's actually fairly easy to avoid Wasteland. If you aren't blowing insane amounts of Pyros, and/or dramatically failing actions involving Pyros, or getting stuck in a rutt, then there's actually very little that causes Wasteland.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> the Role of Soldier is completed when you beat a superior foe, either with force of arms, or with stratagem and cunning. You might get an opportunity soon enough. I don't think we'll go after Mudbreaker in the immediate future, since where she's going is absurdly dangerous, even for Titans and Furies. Werewolves aren't slouches by any stretch of the imagination, and should never be taken lightly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> there will be an opportunity to insert Prime into the story soon enough.<br /> <br /> I'll get the update up, and then we'll see where things go from here. The priorities right now are Amalgama LTD, get some Milestones and Aspirations under your belt, and then moving the story forwards into a larger, High Strangeness direction. I have plans, and the mystery of the Divine Fire and the Principle figures prominently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:01:05-08:00","id":1031800,"title":"","content":"Ah, I wondered if it was tied to his Mission. Got the two mixed up somehow.<br /> That works well, <i>especially </i>if Mark 5 develops some sort of mother hen feelings for his groups and changes to Aes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:06:01-08:00","id":1031863,"title":"","content":"Aes is real good, I've been hoping someone develops it once we get the brand. I like powers that get better with a group, it helps the sense that we're not just a bunch of disconnected randos.<br /> <br /> I just kinda moved things along in my post, I assume we can share philosophies and stuff a little further down the line. Is there anything the rest of y'all want to do before we move on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:22:46-08:00","id":1031872,"title":"","content":"Do I need to add a persuasion roll to my post so that Adonis can get more information about Amalgama Ltd. from Erwin? Or could I resolve Connected to obtain it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T10:59:59-08:00","id":1032212,"title":"","content":"Here's what I'm thinking for extended actions. After their experience with alchemists and her musings about the origin of the Oodena Circle, maybe an Occult research roll to learn &quot;how do humans manipulate the Divine Fire?&quot; Specifically getting useful information about combating alchemists would be good, or other interesting tidbits. I mentioned this in the pre-game thread, but I'd love to explore whether Louis Riel interacted with the Fire somehow and look for rumors in that direction. Could I do that as Manipulation+Occult by talking to others from the Ramble over the next few weeks, adding my Connected bonus? What would be a target number of successes?<br /> <br /> Also, I want to lurk in the North End and establish experience as a vigilante. Getting to know the area, looking for fights, learning exactly what makes her angry and what's satisfying to vent it on. I think she'd be hanging out in a train yard in the general vicinity of the community garden. I don't know if I need to roll for that necessarily, maybe Presence+Intimidation to build up her reputation and establish a bonus to relevant rolls in the neighborhood?<br /> <br /> e: this also might be a good excuse to say that Earth tags along with Scout to check out the cathedral one day while he's researching it, and hits her Elpis Aspiration there. Unless you want to do that in real time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 01-15-2017, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T11:09:32-08:00","id":1032222,"title":"","content":"atm unsure regarding extended rolls. Depending on what the Throng decides on going for next, it'd be either learn more about how to combat vampires, or investigate a bit about Amalgama.<br /> And his general heroing, by intervening in what looks like a crime scene and bluntly asking what's happening and why. He still gives out harsh punishments when he does, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:24:44-08:00","id":1032642,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> rolls are really only called for if it would be interesting if you failed. I also wouldn't have you resolve Connected, because that would mean burning some of your bridges with Erwin, which probably isn't ideal, considering he's the focus of Adonis' current Role. So I have a proposal. You can take the Informed (Amalgama LTD) Condition, but you also take the Disquieted (Erwin) Condition. This won't really cause many problems unless you want the Beats from Disquieted, and Connected will offset it for a while, but it means a little added drama, and Disquiet gets put in play. It's entirely up to you, but I personally think this is the more interesting option.<br /> <br /> If you want to do more &quot;on the ground&quot; research about Amalgama, then a roll of Presence or Manipulation + Persuasion/Politics/Streetwise would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> You can definitely resolve your Elpis Aspiration at the burned out church with Scout, just let me know how that resolved.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> the target number for a roll to research how humans use the Divine Fire is 15 successes. This would be an Intelligence + Occult roll with a bonus from your Library. Target number from researching Louis Riel's more obscure aspects is also 15 successes, and that can definitely be a roll of Manipulation + Occult with the bonus from Connected added in.<br /> <br /> If you'd like to establish yourself as a vigilante, I could see Strength/Presence + Intimidation/Streetwise to be appropriate. Take a penalty to the dice roll equal to the bonus you'd like for rolls pertaining to your vigilante reputation in the future.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> if you're unsure, just hang around and wait. If you want to do some general heroics, Strength + Streetwise would be appropriate. Take a penalty to the roll equal to the bonus you'd like for rolls involving your vigilantism in the future.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> rolling Intelligence + Occult with a target number of 15 will give you information on Amalgama's supernatural/conspiracy goings-on. Rolling Intelligence + Politics/Academics with a target number of 5 will give you information about their corporate actions. Rolling Intelligence + Streetwise with a target number of 15 will give you information about their illegal practices.<br /> <br /> Rolling Intelligence + Academics with a target number of 5 will give you the actual historical articles on the burning of the Saint Boniface Cathedral. Intelligence + Occult with a target number of 10 will give you some supernatural rumours.<br /> <br /> Roll Intelligence + Academics - Desired Map Equipment Bonus to find a suitable map.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:42:16-08:00","id":1032764,"title":"","content":"Updated my last post with stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T19:57:34-08:00","id":1033105,"title":"","content":"It was excellent stuff! I'll update tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> where are you at?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:03:36-08:00","id":1033108,"title":"","content":"Sorry, many things are happening at once both online and RL. Will post Regret's next actions and rolls tonight.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a>, I noticed you also haven't made extended actions. Would you be alright if Regret tagged along to be your sidekick for the extended actions? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Update 01-17-2017, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T22:43:45-08:00","id":1033169,"title":"","content":"Sure, sounds good to me!<br /> <br /> Will roll tonight, about 14 hours from now! Sorry for the wait","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T23:49:56-08:00","id":1033186,"title":"","content":"No worries, I'll post Regret's conclusion of the Ramble tonight and hint that he'll look for Mark 5 in the morning in the area he mentioned he looked after. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> UPDATE: Well, it looks like I'm going to need to make at least one roll of my own after all. It's too late on my end right now, so with your direction <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> what would be the roll to steal some new pens and batteries? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Update 01-17-2017, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T07:02:35-08:00","id":1033335,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> How much time will scout be looking at per roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T07:57:26-08:00","id":1033358,"title":"","content":"I figured most were once a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:47:15-08:00","id":1033388,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> if you just want to grab batteries and pens, I wouldn't call for a roll. You can just get that done, maybe establish a Disquiet Condition for a particular region of the city where you were stealing from. No point giving a chance of failure if the failure wouldn't be interesting. You also can get Equipment using the Availability rules, which more or less follow the rules for Resources/Status/Allies.<br /> <br /> That said, if you wanted to gather up some <i>more </i>Equipment, then I would say you could roll Wits/Dexterity/Manipulation (depending on your approach) + Larceny - the total Availability of the Equipment you want to gather to see if you can steal it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> I was thinking that each roll would take up the better part of a day, but time is mostly inconsequential. The interlude period of the time skip is going to be a couple of weeks, so it doesn't really matter how long each of your actions take, so long as you take your actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:20:08-08:00","id":1033432,"title":"","content":"I'll go with the simple snatching meathod for now. Regret wouldn't be interested in any extra equipment atm, plus setting up the first stages of Disquiet in a dramatically plot relevant place sounds like a better plan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:21:56-08:00","id":1033486,"title":"","content":"I think that was 30-31 rolls, all told. Scout has been a busy person. *is glad he didn't have to physically roll all those dice*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:09:57-08:00","id":1033670,"title":"","content":"Added a Persuasion roll to my previous post. I'll add some rolls to my most current post when I have the chance. Adonis and Scout might end up being roomies, if this keeps up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T16:44:32-08:00","id":1033726,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> the persuasion roll wasn't strictly necessary, but it is good to see. I definitely think you should roll for Disquiet.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> just for future reference, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> mentioned, I'm treating Equipment Building rolls as a single, abstracted, dice pool as per the subsystem on <b>Chronicles of Darkness pg. 100</b> Basically, the new subsystem lets you build any kind of Equipment, that offers any kind of dice bonus, by building a single, suitable, dice pool, and rolling. Penalties can be spent on dice bonuses or other special traits, same way penalties can be spent on Spell Factors in Mage 2E.<br /> <br /> Pass or fail, you get the Equipment, but you get delicious complications (and Conditions) from Failure. The only way you don't get the Equipment, at all, is Dramatic Failure. Either way, Mark 5 gets his reputation, which works. Earth gets a much scarier reputation though.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> that's a whole lot to process! I'm going to take my time going through that, because I really want to get all the details right, and you're going to start getting into High Strangeness stuff relatively soon. Expect lots of Divine Fire weirdness. This is going to be good. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> would I be correct in assuming the question you asked with the use of Pilgrim's Landmark was to find an Elpis Vision Athanor? Because Earth got her Elpis Vision from an Elpis Aspiration tied to the Vivid Dreams Merit.<br /> <br /> As a side note, can I just say how pleased I am that some of you are <i>opting </i>to throw in Disquiet? Not just because it leads to easy Beat farming, but also because it adds some lovely drama to Promethean. Besides, Earth won't really get to stretch her wings as a Fury (nor Regret or Scout as Originists) if there isn't any Disquiet to manipulate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:10:48-08:00","id":1033743,"title":"","content":"Since you mentioned using the Torches and Pitchforks rules earlier, I wanted to start bringing that kind of drama and consequences front and center. I was thinking about rolling for Church Lady disquiet, but figured she was just a walk-on character. I'm totally okay declaring she's at Stage 1 now if you like though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:37:55-08:00","id":1033761,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> Added the Disquiet roll. And once again, no successes. At the rate this is going, Erwin might find himself becoming a dot in True Friend! Speaking of which, I think going out to dinner with Erwin and sleeping with him qualifies as Adonis fulfilling his Aspiration to go on a date. May I have a Beat, pretty please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, what is the Elpis Aspiration? I can't seem to find anything about that in the book. Do you mean acting on his Elpis? Or are you talking about including rolls for the Elpis Vision?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:58:22-08:00","id":1033770,"title":"","content":"I have the Vivid Dreams merit, which gives me another Aspiration slot that triggers an elpis vision when I hit it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:39:36-08:00","id":1034079,"title":"","content":"I am still not as familiar with the rules as I'd like to, due to RL work, sorry!<br /> Also, kinda forgot that opting for Disquiet even is a thing. Hm... =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:57:23-08:00","id":1034228,"title":"","content":"With Pilgrim's mark he's trying to find athanors in general in the area. The elpis vision was him trying to force one with the athanors of the missing prometheans.<br /> <br /> Edit: Should I go ahead and respond to Adonis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 01-18-2017, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:14:29-08:00","id":1034339,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> go ahead, it doesn't have much bearing on the plot, but it's more character interaction and that's what I like to see.<br /> <br /> More importantly, this update is going to be massive. I think I'm going to have to tackle it in stages, starting with Adonis, Regret, and Mark 5 before moving on to Scout and Earth.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> you can definitely gain a Beat from that Aspiration, and I'd also take three Vitriol Beats from that. It's a fairly progressive Milestone in terms of understanding the Role of Companion.<br /> \u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> don't forget to mark the three Vitriol Beats from the Milestone you just experienced.<br /> \u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> is there a particular person you wanted to inflict with Disquiet? I figured something more abstract like Disquiet (North End) [Stage 1] would be appropriate. For the Torches and Pitchforks stuff, I'll be using each stage of Disquiet as a die in the pool. Success leads to the Watched Condition for the group, which would then resolve into Surveilled or Hunted, as appropriate.<br /> <br /> And the result of Tension is... <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=b47dc98f\" target=\"_blank\">nobody is coming after you</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-18-2017, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:39:58-08:00","id":1034349,"title":"","content":"Yeah given her reputation, it seems good to assume North End NPCs who know about her have a general Disquiet. Something isn't right about her, even if they see her out of disguise. Note that she's avoiding the community garden until she resolves Disconnected. I was just suggesting that if we wanted to introduce a particular troublesome recurring mortal, it could also be possible to have Disquieted the woman at the church, since she knows who Earth and Scout are. &quot;Those weird ugly siblings I saw hanging around!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:50:48-08:00","id":1034565,"title":"","content":"I already had 2, so I added them up to one vitriolic experience. Should I Note that in the header, keeping it as 5/5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:58:13-08:00","id":1034570,"title":"","content":"Not necessary. Just keep in mind that you have the Vitriol Experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:36:11-08:00","id":1034588,"title":"","content":"Arcanist if you want to write a little less at once, maybe you could break up Earth and Scout's stuff into halves we can respond to? Like the elpis visions could be interactive in some way if that suits your plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:48:53-08:00","id":1034599,"title":"","content":"That will work. I'm actually working on the updates for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> right now. Was planning on handling Earth and Scout's posts individually just due to the sheer volume of stuff. Will release it in bits and pieces.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Update for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> is up. Just a warning, we're starting to get into some of the ugly stuff in the city. You don't have to go down the rabbit hole, but you can if you want to explore it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-19-2017, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:01:17-08:00","id":1034911,"title":"","content":"Quick update everyone. I'll be going on a camping trip from the 20-22 so I don't think I'll be able to post until I get back. I'll catch up on the updates now and give Regret's general mindset and aspirations so if Mark 5 and Adonis want to advance the plot you can NPC Regret if need be Arcanist.<br /> <br /> UPDATE: Love the write up, Regret will stand behind Mark 5's decision no matter what. His residual memories will slide too easily back into the soldier mentality so his approach to the Gang's facility would be to scout it for several days and then try to cut off their supply lines. Try and discover who goes in and out, and generally use gorilla tactics like that. What rolls would you recommend for that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Update 01-20-2017, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:48:05-08:00","id":1035249,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> I would say Wits + Streetwise. If you want to make it a Building Equipment roll, take a penalty equal to the Equipment Bonus you want, otherwise make an Extended Action roll with a target number of five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:55:27-08:00","id":1035285,"title":"","content":"What should I roll for trying to reduce IP activity? Like ambushing groups of them, force them to cut down on their presence, or even take out a weapon stash or hideout, stuff like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:36:37-08:00","id":1035335,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> well, I would consider it a Social Maneuvering Action, probably involving Hard Leverage, but I'll have to figure out what the Violence Group traits for IP would be. Let me get back to you on that, it shouldn't take too too long. There are also rules for this sort of thing in <b>Chronicles of Darkness: The Hurt Locker </b>which I'll have to review, but I'll give you the rundown when I'm ready. The whole thing is intended to be an opportunity for character growth to both Mark 5 and to Regret, so we'll see how it goes.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> your monster of an update is up! I had a lot of stuff to write out, and I think it paid off. Hopefully you enjoy. I tried to go a little abstract and surreal with the Elpis Vision, giving you a chance to interpret it for yourself, but I <i>did </i>answer your question.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> I'm getting to Earth's update next. I'm hoping to finish it today, but worst case scenario I'll get it out tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T17:07:59-08:00","id":1035530,"title":"","content":"To quote a friend... that was intense! I feel like I'm going to spend all weekend parsing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T03:39:01-08:00","id":1035670,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a><br /> No worries, take your time! =) I thought this is a perfect opportunity to explore the &quot;Hero&quot; lifestyle, and possibly the ripples it causes, too =D<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T20:34:41-08:00","id":1035932,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Earth's beast of an update is finally done! Man, there was a lot of stuff to cover. Note to self, make the next time skip a little smaller. Or write more quickly, one of the two.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> everyone has been updated and the story can move forwards! How do you guys react to your interlude actions, and where and why do you all meet up again?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> for IP, you will need to open a total of seven Doors in a Social Maneuvering action. You have a Hostile Impression with them, so you can't take a regular Social Maneuvering action. Your only option right now is to Force Doors or use Hard Leverage. However, you could use other rolls to figure out their Vice, their group Aspirations, that sort of thing, and use Soft Leverage to open negotiations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-21-2017, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T20:37:50-08:00","id":1035934,"title":"","content":"Jeepers, that's a lot of quality #content! Thank you for writing at such length, seriously, I'm so grateful you're putting so much of your time and creativity into this game as ST.<br /> <br /> Real quick: is this a chapter break for power-recharge and beat-gain purposes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T21:21:11-08:00","id":1035945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1035934#post1035934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeepers, that's a lot of quality #content! Thank you for writing at such length, seriously, I'm so grateful you're putting so much of your time and creativity into this game as ST.<br /> <br /> Real quick: is this a chapter break for power-recharge and beat-gain purposes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm glad to be your ST! Earth and the others are great characters, and Promethean is a fabulous game to write for. The funny thing about creativity, is when you use it, it grows back faster and thicker, like some rather lovely shrub. This is indeed considered a proper chapter break for power-recharge and beat-gain purposes.<br /> <br /> How did you find the Elpis Visions? Too abstract or surrealist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T22:04:58-08:00","id":1035955,"title":"","content":"I really like Earth's. Echoing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> that I'm gonna be parsing and interpreting it for a while. I like the contrast between the really grounded side of North End crime and the Red River Rebellion versus the weird Pyros-world that the Created live in, it sort of reinforces how our characters are outsiders to mundane humanity. It's fun to read and think about and work through and the imagery will definitely be on my mind this weekend. The lacuna-feast is incredibly disturbing body horror that succeeded in grossing me out in a good way- it puts me in the right mindset by establishing that Earth has done some really vile things even if they aren't highlighted in detail in the present. It's not an abstract &quot;she a villain&quot; thing, but a shocking and inhuman sensory experience. I also really enjoy the image of the Pyros-entity with the broad shoulders (!) and blackened hand, I'm looking forward to deciding what Earth thinks that was about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998318-ic-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1035931#post1035931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More <b>mOcKERy</b> and she won't stand for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for bringing that in, haha. I like playing with the text medium that way. <a href=\"http://www.marlborotech.com/Zalgo.html\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> is where I did Earth's t\u030f\u0315\u0339\u0323o\u031a\u0304\u0357\u036a\u0344\u0306\u0321\u032c\u034d\u0330r\u0312\u0366\u0305\u0303\u0489\u0359\u0345\u0316m\u036f\u0304\u036d\u036e\u0328\u0358\u0348\u0339\u032a\u0348\u0332e\u0301\u036d\u0336\u0328\u0321\u0330\u034e\u0347\u032f\u031c\u0326\u031c \u0356\u033cn\u0306\u0305\u0343\u0309\u030a\u0343\u0361\u0340\u0353\u032f\u0345\u0317\u035at\u0364\u0357\u0309\u0337\u0341\u0355\u0323 \u0313\u036d\u031a\u030e\u036f\u0334\u0330\u0333\u0345\u033a\u0354\u0326\u0316v\u0343\u036d\u036a\u030c\u030e\u0355\u032b\u0349\u0319\u031d\u031c\u0349\u0330\u032co\u030e\u0311\u030c\u0367\u035b\u0362\u0361\u0334\u0333\u0354\u0317\u032f\u0319\u034d\u0333\u0318i\u0369\u0365\u0327\u0338 \u0333\u032f\u0348c\u033f\u0351\u036f\u0367\u0350\u0327\u0326\u035a\u0347\u0326\u0354\u0359e\u030d\u030d\u0364\u0367\u0314\u030c\u0357\u0364\u0309\u0335\u0337\u0315\u031c\u0323\u032f\u0339\u0325 last time, if you ever want to mess with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T00:27:43-08:00","id":1035977,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> I can only subscribe to what has already been said: loving the work you put in here!<br /> <br /> So, in regards to Mark 5 and the IP, since 'Heroes don't negotiate', and he <i>finally </i>has found a group that actually is evil enough in their intent and action to warrant his attention, I think we should go for hard leverage here, with the Titan attacking them and threatening that he will keep coming after them if they do not stop &quot;their wrongdoings&quot;.<br /> I think it would be nice to explore the more ruthless part of Mark 5 here (his Torment is, after all, Merciless for a reason) and I think I will roll for Disquiet because a group being constantly harrassed by a Promethean feels like an appropriate situation.<br /> <br /> What should I roll for the Hard Leverage (Presence+Intimidation?) and should/could I roll for Torment due to his brutality in hunting down IP members?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:50:50-08:00","id":1036365,"title":"","content":"Hey all, will catch up on what's transpired and idealistically post Regret's response and actions later tonight once I get home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:31:14-08:00","id":1036649,"title":"","content":"I am still mind blown over just how much quality content you are dropping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:00:09-08:00","id":1036717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1035955#post1035955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like Earth's. Echoing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> that I'm gonna be parsing and interpreting it for a while. I like the contrast between the really grounded side of North End crime and the Red River Rebellion versus the weird Pyros-world that the Created live in, it sort of reinforces how our characters are outsiders to mundane humanity. It's fun to read and think about and work through and the imagery will definitely be on my mind this weekend. The lacuna-feast is incredibly disturbing body horror that succeeded in grossing me out in a good way- it puts me in the right mindset by establishing that Earth has done some really vile things even if they aren't highlighted in detail in the present. It's not an abstract &quot;she a villain&quot; thing, but a shocking and inhuman sensory experience. I also really enjoy the image of the Pyros-entity with the broad shoulders (!) and blackened hand, I'm looking forward to deciding what Earth thinks that was about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for bringing that in, haha. I like playing with the text medium that way. <a href=\"http://www.marlborotech.com/Zalgo.html\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> is where I did Earth's t\u0339\u0323\u030f\u0315\u014d\u0321\u032c\u034d\u0330\u0357\u036a\u0308\u0301\u0306\u031ar\u0312\u0366\u0305\u0303\u0489\u0359\u0316\u0345m\u0328\u0348\u0339\u032a\u0348\u0332\u036f\u0304\u036d\u036e\u0358\u0119\u0336\u0321\u0330\u034e\u0347\u032f\u031c\u0326\u031c\u0301\u036d \u0356\u033cn\u0353\u032f\u0317\u035a\u0306\u0305\u0313\u0309\u030a\u0313\u0300\u0361\u0345t\u0337\u0355\u0323\u0364\u0357\u0309\u0301 \u0334\u0330\u0333\u033a\u0354\u0326\u0316\u0313\u036d\u030e\u036f\u031a\u0345v\u0355\u032b\u0349\u0319\u031d\u031c\u0349\u0330\u032c\u0313\u036d\u036a\u030c\u030eo\u0334\u0333\u0354\u0317\u032f\u0319\u034d\u0333\u0318\u030e\u0311\u030c\u0367\u035b\u0362\u0361i\u0338\u0327\u0369\u0365 \u0333\u032f\u0348\u00e7\u0326\u035a\u0347\u0326\u0354\u0359\u033f\u0351\u036f\u0367\u0350e\u0335\u0337\u031c\u0323\u032f\u0339\u0325\u030d\u030d\u0364\u0367\u0314\u030c\u0357\u0364\u0309\u0315 last time, if you ever want to mess with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool feature! I'll have to keep that one in the back of my head for later, and I can't help but think it would be really useful for a Demon game, especially when a character has low Cover or Goes Loud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:28:05-08:00","id":1036735,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> no problem, take your time. There's a lot to process.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> The very nature of Hard Leverage will mean that you would have to make a Breaking Point roll. Your base dice pool is 5. If you take a -2 penalty to the dice pool due to more horrific and merciless action, you'll open <i>two </i>Doors, which would leave you with another five to open. I would also suggest that you roll for Torment after that, which is Resolve + Composure - Azoth. There is no need to roll for Hard Leverage to succeed, it just works.<br /> <br /> Now, if you wanted to Force Doors, on the other hand, that would be a rolled action. I would suggest Strength + Intimidation. The penalty to Forcing Doors is the current number of Doors left, so it would be a flat penalty of -7 to begin with, or -5 with Hard Leverage. You can take additional Hard Leverage actions, but it would mean more Breaking Points. If you accepted the Tormented Condition, however, as a result of your Hard Leverage action, then not only would you earn a Beat, but you could open three Doors instead.<br /> <br /> For Disquiet, roll Azoth. Uh, <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=b64c4709\" target=\"_blank\">holy crap.</a> It appears as though the gangsters not only resisted Disquiet, but are completely immune to Disquiet for the rest of the Chapter unless you get six successes on a dice pool of two?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> Promethean is a well of deep Storytelling and inspiration that I have been thinking about for a long time but had never really managed to tap into through a game. It's also in this weird spot of patchwork urban fantasy, horror, and dark whimsy that my particular brand of writing is great at capturing. Also, Winnipeg has a really fascinating history that I can tap and that keeps getting stranger as it unfolds.<br /> <br /> For example, we were subject to Nazi invasion in WWII. For a few days, Manitoba was occupied by Nazi Germany, and then a group looking to drum up support for wartime donations came forwards and said &quot;this is what other people are living with. Donate money to stop it.&quot; This project was called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/If_Day\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;If</a> <a href=\"http://www.pastperfectpro.com/films/page7/ifday.html\" target=\"_blank\">Day.&quot; </a>People were told about it in advance to avoid widespread panic, but much like the War of the Worlds broadcast, it still caught people by surprise and convinced them it was real.<br /> <br /> I'm glad for all the complements though, and I'm happy everyone is enjoying the story so far. Don't worry! Weirdness is coming! Prepare to get less grounded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T13:32:12-08:00","id":1036797,"title":"","content":"Holy crap, that Breaking Point roll sounds interesting. Kinda makes me hope it fails, same with Torment, to get a &quot;Going down the slippery slope&quot; as &quot;He who fights Monsters...&quot; kind of feeling...<br /> ESPECIALLY if it succeeds in doing Good, that would result in some serious need for introspection...<br /> Will think that over, thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T01:06:12-08:00","id":1037082,"title":"","content":"Let's shift gears back to shorter and less draining posts for a while after this! This has been a climactic and cool end to the chapter with great character spotlights, but I'm ready to dial it back and not establish life philosophies in every post.<br /> <br /> I suggest everyone congregates at a diner on (arbitrary date: Sunday, December 4th?) to compare notes and decide where we go next. When I think Promethean, I think greasy spoon diners and Disquieted customers leering at the weirdos in the corner booth. Plus I wanna get some poutine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1036735#post1036735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, we were subject to Nazi invasion in WWII. For a few days, Manitoba was occupied by Nazi Germany, and then a group looking to drum up support for wartime donations came forwards and said &quot;this is what other people are living with. Donate money to stop it.&quot; This project was called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/If_Day\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;If</a> <a href=\"http://www.pastperfectpro.com/films/page7/ifday.html\" target=\"_blank\">Day.&quot; </a>People were told about it in advance to avoid widespread panic, but much like the War of the Worlds broadcast, it still caught people by surprise and convinced them it was real.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had never heard about that, that's really interesting.<br /> <br /> Random image on my mind today: a Promethean with Electrification, employed/imprisoned powering the generator for some dodgy compound out in the winter wilderness. Like a low-budget Arisen cult that isn't expecting their master back any time soon, that would be a cool bit of background flavor. Something for one of us following Stannum at the time to do during a timeskip, maybe, or some NPC we can seek out to rescue or punish. I'm a big fan of semi-clued in mortals who stumble onto a source of Real Mystical Power and use it for the pettiest reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 01-24-2017, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:20:40-08:00","id":1037155,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I intend fully to go back to regular gameplay now. The big, huge, philosophical posts are awesome to write and (I hope) equally fun to read, but they're draining, take a lot of time, and would slow game progression to a crawl, so I'll try and avoid those for a little bit.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> the High Weirdness imagery is noted. I'll find ways to incorporate things like that in the game relatively soon. Also, if the Throng is going to be meeting up at a diner, may I suggest local favourite <a href=\"https://www.zomato.com/winnipeg-mb/red-top-drive-inn-winnipeg/info\" target=\"_blank\">Red Top</a>? Not quite a greasy spoon, but it's close enough. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> don't know where you're at, but I know you commented here recently. Just letting you know that we've got the All Clear and can move forwards with the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:51:09-08:00","id":1037169,"title":"","content":"I did a &quot;processing&quot; post for Scout to try and start thinking things through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:03:29-08:00","id":1037383,"title":"","content":"Will write a short post regarding the IP thing tomorrow. Depending on how that turns out, the Throng might have to deal with a Tormented Titan upon meeting up =D<br /> <br /> Edit: If I accept Torment as a consequence of Hard Leverage, Mark 5 gets to open 3 doors without a roll, do I read that correctly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 01-25-2017, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T17:37:17-08:00","id":1039175,"title":"","content":"Alright, that took way longer than I thought but fully up to speed now. Love the events that have transpired so far. Have a few questions for what I kinda see Regret doing next, will need your advice @Arcanist.<br /> <br /> 1) Definitly going to make a building equipment roll for what I'm calling Fabien Tactics (containing IP rather than fighting them head on), may I spend willpower for heroic effort or is this a Extended Action roll?<br /> <br /> 2) Will definitly start worrying when Mark 5 sorta breaks off communications and goes Rambo on IP, would it require a roll to see what's happening or if there's any way Regret can mitigate some of the damage done from his Torment? (Just like Frank did with Regret.)<br /> <br /> 3) Is there an opportunity for Regret to make progress towards one of his Roles (Chronicler) by observing Mark 5 slowly descent into Torment after weeks of fighting against IP? <br /> <br /> Also, depending on how the rolls go Regret might be the bearer of bad news regarding Mark 5's absense from the agreed upon meeting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 01-27-2017, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:39:55-08:00","id":1039793,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> I'll answer these one at a time.<br /> <br /> 1) It's a single Instant Action representing an abstract period of time. Assemble a dice pool for that, apply a -2 penalty due to Disquiet, and apply a penalty equal to the Equipment Bonus you want for the Equipment. You can definitely spend Willpower on it. Because it's tactics, and a plan, the Equipment could apply to Mark 5 as well.<br /> <br /> 2) I wouldn't say you need a roll to figure out what's happening. It's clear enough. Mark 5 isn't making as much of a splash as Earth is, but he's still building a reputation. He's known in the local community now as Breaker, a troubleshooter who likes to handle gangbangers with his fists and seems to be as strong and fast as a human can be. If you want to mitigate the damage and the rumours, that's a different story. That would be an Extended Manipulation + Stealth roll, with a target number of five. If you want to start an alternative rumour to keep trouble off of Mark 5's back and deflect blame to a different gang, that would be Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Presence + Composure (which would be a total of four dice, for the Presence + Composure pool).<br /> <br /> 3) Absolutely. Just need to explain Regret's thought process, how it relates to his Pilgrimage, and how it relates to his own perspective and philosophy, such as it is. I imagine that the Dead Soliders will have something to say about what they're seeing. (And I absolutely love that you're going the route of having the history of the bodies that went into making Regret have a lasting impact on him)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T21:28:10-08:00","id":1039817,"title":"","content":"This is kinda cool: the line developer for Promethean has been posting <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?619795-Promethean-The-Created-The-7th-Angel/page5\" target=\"_blank\">play reports</a> of his home game on and off for the last few years. The last 2 posts are them updating to 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T00:53:54-08:00","id":1039875,"title":"","content":"Heh, Regret 'babysitting' Mark 5 is cool. I like the dynamic that's building up there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 