od","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T13:00:42-08:00","id":1044147,"title":"","content":"Here's what I suggest we do next! Track down Mark 5, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> uses Heed the Call to take Mark's Measure and learn his Elpis in-character, and then we do something cool to try to trigger his Elpis. Maybe bringing him along to fight the Pandorans in the catacombs, and hope he displays Courage in the process?<br /> <br /> I also think it would be really cool for Earth to first try and brawl with Mark and try to burn his Torment off that way, and <i>completely</i> get her ass kicked, but only if the rest of the group is willing to indulge 3 or 4 turns of punching. I just wanna do something quick on-screen to establish what we were talking about back in the recruitment thread, where the two Tammuz have a strength differential and there's some tension there. There also might be a Milestone in having a friendly fight that teaches limits.<br /> <br /> e: totally forgot you can also just try to resolve Torment directly with Heed the Call, although it's risky. not my decision to make, just laying out some of the tools the throng has available","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of