 azoth he used? Will that require a roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T09:18:14-08:00","id":1157564,"title":"","content":"Adonis getting a really badass scene here, I like it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T04:35:51-08:00","id":1182873,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, It's been a while. Are all of you alright?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T09:23:33-08:00","id":1184768,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> so, I'm not dead, but life did its level best to make me that way. I owe you guys an explanation. My practicum last term did not go well. My teacher mentor was reaping the consequences of bad personal life decisions, and he took it out on me. I wasn't his kind of teacher, so there was personal friction mixed with &quot;my way or the highway&quot; attitude. I got by on the skin of my teeth, and on top of that my home situation took a bit of a turn for the worst. Took all my energy just to keep moving forwards.<br /> <br /> I'm significantly better now, and itching with stories to tell. If you'll have me back, I'm ready to continue Muddy Waters.<br /> <br /> Also, someone new requested to join the game as a Promethean rescued in the attack on Amalgama, so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"20770\" data-vbnamecard=\"20770\">Caius Wickersham</a> you get a notice too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T13:42:45-08:00","id":1184873,"title":"","content":"Well, I might as well introduce myself. I've been wanting to play Promethean for a while and I saw this game up. I asked Arcanist if he had extra room and we've been discussing my coming in since November (obviously some give and take there with his busy schedule). I hope I can fit in with the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham","name":"Caius Wickersham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T07:49:31-08:00","id":1185175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1184768#post1184768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> so, I'm not dead, but life did its level best to make me that way. I owe you guys an explanation. My practicum last term did not go well. My teacher mentor was reaping the consequences of bad personal life decisions, and he took it out on me. I wasn't his kind of teacher, so there was personal friction mixed with &quot;my way or the highway&quot; attitude. I got by on the skin of my teeth, and on top of that my home situation took a bit of a turn for the worst. Took all my energy just to keep moving forwards.<br /> <br /> I'm significantly better now, and itching with stories to tell. If you'll have me back, I'm ready to continue Muddy Waters.<br /> <br /> Also, someone new requested to join the game as a Promethean rescued in the attack on Amalgama, so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"20770\" data-vbnamecard=\"20770\">Caius Wickersham</a> you get a notice too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey man, sorry to hear that! I can very much imagine what that's like. Glad to hear you're alright!<br /> Well, I'd be thrilled to continue, at the very least =) People disappearing for a while is simply one of the dangers of PbP, due to the amount of time a game takes. I'm sure the others feel the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"20770\" data-vbnamecard=\"20770\">Caius Wickersham</a> Hey Caius, sounds good to me. What did you have in mind for your char?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T09:17:39-08:00","id":1185223,"title":"","content":"My guy is an Osiran currently on the Plumbum Transmutation (I picked up the Alembic for making a branded throng as well). My image of him is essentially a Promethean scientist, studying Prometheans and all their strange bits along with humanity. He's also got some survival skills thanks to coming out of the lake country east of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham","name":"Caius Wickersham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T00:29:21-08:00","id":1185512,"title":"","content":"Welcome back! And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"20770\" data-vbnamecard=\"20770\">Caius Wickersham</a> welcome aboard!<br /> <br /> I like these characters and I still wanna play with whoever's around, but I don't wanna get bogged down in scenes we're not having fun with. Can I make some suggestions?<ul><li>I think we should have Arcanist briefly narrate us to the end of the Amalgama raid, rather than picking up where we left off. If there's a big scene you really want to play out at Amalgama, like a villain speech or complex skill roll or Milestone, we can jump right into that and bite into something fun before moving on to the next story with our new PC.</li> <li>I would like it across the board if we did more broad, light, fast-moving stuff and fewer dense dialogue/conversation updates, at least until we're in a good groove again. I'm in a Mage game right now that has really good pacing; we talk more conversationally with the ST about what we're doing and then &quot;zoom in&quot; on interesting stuff to play it out in-character, rather than treating everything as a full scene. It would be cool to do something similar-ish like at the beginning of this game, when it was more brief updates saying what we're doing and only getting denser when interesting stuff is happening. Shorter lighter posts and scenes with a clear sense of what's going on are good habits for PBP!</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T06:10:01-08:00","id":1185554,"title":"","content":"Welcome back. I'm still ready to rock. I am really hoping to have Scout find the amalgama lab and it's gadgets, as the study of pyros and creating things is his big thing, and he is still in torment so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T06:28:47-08:00","id":1185926,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> about the epilogue for Amalgama. No sense diving back into an action scene months after the fact. I also agree with the game turning a little more conversational, because that allows character to develop and I really enjoy the idea of that. (Also, more opportunity for me to introduce characters. Yay! I've got a <i>lot </i>of stuff in my back pocket) Let me double check my notes and I'll be back in a few days with an epilogue to the raid all set to go and we can carry on from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T04:14:54-08:00","id":1188126,"title":"","content":"Holy crap! What is dead may never die!<br /> <br /> I'm very sorry guys, family issues and the start of a much-busier semester took me by surprise. I haven't even been active on the forums. But this morning I decided to check in on a whim and I'm very glad I did. <br /> <br /> Yes, I am fine with us skipping past the Amalgama fight, it would be super strange to drop us back into the middle of a combat after several months. I am a firm &quot;ready to go.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T07:40:48-08:00","id":1188171,"title":"","content":"So, looks like we got the whole crew back together. I was beginning to worry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham","name":"Caius Wickersham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T11:08:46-08:00","id":1188234,"title":"","content":"Give me another day to edit the stuff I have going for an epilogue and then we'll be back on track.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"20770\" data-vbnamecard=\"20770\">Caius Wickersham</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> we're back online! I've left some neat Storytelling opportunities open, and figured that a time skip sort of needed to happen. Feel free to spend any and all Experiences you've accrued, just let me know what the result is.<br /> <br /> Also, feel free to give me a refresher on your Aspirations so I remember to incorporate them more this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 02-22-2018, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T12:04:48-08:00","id":1188598,"title":"","content":"I feel like Scout has been spending his time researching the Rebis, and perhaps has attempted to make contact with The Concordance. I think he's probably started trying to make his own creations by now- especially after having seen the 'wonders' of the amalgama labs that night. Trying his hand to see if he can actually create something new, a sort of stepping stone on the path to the New Dawn. I'd love if he'd be able to have made some sort of gadget or another, but I'm not sure what sort of thing fits. I am also not sure how much more progress he'd have made in researching the Rebis or making contact with The Concordance.<br /> <br /> Depending on how those events go will let me know if he'd have completed the Ascetic role- especially if he successfully creates some sort of invention of his own. If I have enough beats from the conditions lapsing, I'll probably get a point in craft to help with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 02-22-2018, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T12:54:04-08:00","id":1188626,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> <br /> I think Mark 5 would be solidly placed on his Cobalus path by now. Due to the combination of his old Path (Ferrum), his condition (Guilty) that partly played a role into picking up Cobalus, and him resolving that, I imagine he's a Confessor with Phobos as his Mesmerism and Suffering for his Contamination.<br /> This places Mark 5 safely out of his comfort and safe zone, as interaction isn't his strongest suit.<br /> He'd be coming back to see if he could find Earth again, and a new Aspiration would be to have Earth open up to him and tell him a secret or confess something else that makes her feel bad.<br /> Also, he'd be coming to see if he could find more clues on Mudbreaker, his creator. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T16:18:34-08:00","id":1188696,"title":"","content":"Okay, with a big timeskip like this, I'm gonna run with an idea I mentioned in the thread way back.<br /> <br /> Earth had a really sucky 2017. Following the Role of the Hermit, they left the city and went north into the wilderness to get their head straight, alone. They visited some of the places where Earth-Dies-Screaming caused a lot of damage, which combined with that Watched condition caused some real trouble. They were tracked down by some very angry humans who knew about the destruction and misery the Centimanus had caused, and captured in Ontario. This turned out to be super bad, because the humans were connected to a cult, and just barely clued-in enough about the supernatural to be dangerous.<br /> <br /> Earth spent months chained up in a survivalist compound, and as Tammuz do, they were put to work. Manual labor, farming food and drug-ready poppies, mechanical repair. Unsuccessful attempts to power their generator with Electrification, despite Earth's furious protests that it &quot;doesn't work that way.&quot; The compound was built around some kind of strange relic that sapped their Pyros and interfered with their Vivid Dreams. Eventually, they sunk into Torment and stopped trying to talk.<br /> <br /> Earth learned bits and pieces of their lore. They called themselves the True Temple of Silence. A bunch of angry lonely men and boys wearing trucker caps and amulets, selling poppies and firearms and waiting for the Sothic Turn, whatever that meant. They talked about an ancient civilization in North America, great magical monuments aligned with the stars, an end to death, the sky-filling Whale Bone Woman and the cyclical return of her earthly avatar. There had been some kind of dispute among the cult in past years, and this faction (the true believers, of course) had stolen a relic and established this compound in exile, waiting obediently for their lord to return when the stars aligned.<br /> <br /> Disquiet and the Wasteland set in. The crops Earth tended were ruined by mudslides and endless black rain. The Temple muttered about their servant, then shouted. Driven by mad urges, they tried to harvest Pyros and Vitriol to resurrect their master, despite having little talent for alchemy. In the darkness of their Babylonian Captivity, Earth thought many times about giving up and descending into Stannum, becoming an Outcast and joining with the humans, or stepping off the path again altogether. Maybe if they had gotten over themself and joined a proper Branded Throng, things would be different. But, driven by the hope of being known to the Principle and the memory of being part of a community in Winnipeg, they stubbornly carried on in Cuprum. That's that Elpis of Faith in action!<br /> <br /> Then one night, Earth saw <a href=\"https://imgur.com/IJknuy0\" target=\"_blank\">the butterflies</a> again. The next day, the wretched Wasteland boiled over, and the Temple was consumed by a Firestorm. Earth escaped.<br /> <br /> After that, they spent some time in the wilderness, taking animal shapes with Metamorphosis. They spent some time in the small towns of Ontario, exchanging a few words every week with humans again. Migrated south to Toronto for the coldest months of winter, learned some new human words. Took rock drumming lessons after answering a flyer in a coffee shop, until Disquiet ruined it.<br /> <br /> Now they've headed back to Winnipeg. They had a vision telling them the Hermit's path would lead them back to the Ramble. The prophet has spent enough time in the wilderness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T19:01:08-08:00","id":1188746,"title":"","content":"Dang! So here I am in Winnipeg getting set up and you all fart off. Oh well, maybe I can have a few adventures to catch myself up to you all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham","name":"Caius Wickersham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T20:50:55-08:00","id":1188766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caius Wickersham</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1188746#post1188746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dang! So here I am in Winnipeg getting set up and you all fart off. Oh well, maybe I can have a few adventures to catch myself up to you all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yo, that's a good point! We're kinda leaving you hanging. We can definitely say that all the current PCs met up after the raid and before we scattered to the winds, exchanged business cards, etc. I just had liked the idea of Earth being off on their own and addressing their Torment for a while, especially as a Hermit, although I can dial it back and be more in contact with everybody in Winnipeg.<br /> <br /> What's Basil all about? If we were sitting around the gaming table for session one, what should we know about him before we start?<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> I'll put the ball in your court for what happened with Adonis and Erwin and the Frozen Pilgrim. Earth got mind-whammy'd and given an Aspiration to push Adonis to confront Erwin, and was also totally enchanted with the Pilgrim, so however that figures into it. I'd been picturing Earth excitedly telling the Pilgrim in person &quot;I see you, I'm listening, just tell me what you want me to do&quot; as a show of Faith in the Principle. We established already that Earth is super envious of how easily Adonis deals with humans, but they're also happy for his relationship and don't want to smash it up, so it could go all kinds of ways. Just clapping their claw on his shoulder while running for cover with a word about &quot;your dude is an alchemist, he isn't like us, how did you even think this was gonna work&quot; would be a good start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T21:07:30-08:00","id":1188771,"title":"","content":"Basil's incredibly new to being a Promethean, but he's got skills to help him survive and join up with other Prometheans. He's incredibly soft-spoken and will begin holding a conversation with himself when something of interest comes to his mind. He's got a large book with him and he's seeking more information about Prometheans and he's got a bit of a flash on Earth. Something tells him there's more to Earth and he wants to know more about her.<br /> <br /> For all the cerebral nature he's got going, he's also very skilled with improvised weapons and capable of outdoor survival, always seeming to know which way he is supposed to go, establish a shelter, and able to eat anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham","name":"Caius Wickersham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T02:41:38-08:00","id":1188812,"title":"","content":"Oh I didn't say he wouldn't come back. Scout will certainly want to share his tale with the group. I'm just needing to get. Clarity on the tale itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T07:23:37-08:00","id":1189217,"title":"","content":"Erwin stuck around in town just long enough to deal with the police. The official story is that he was working on a metal-organic framework in the lab when it caught fire. It helped that Adonis' &quot;friend&quot; on the force was amenable to making sure the story took root. Then, after brief farewells to his unofficial Throng, Adonis vanished with his alchemist boyfriend into the night. <br /> <br /> They spent a few weeks on the road, driving across the Canadian prairies and holing up in dingy motel rooms that they never seemed to get charged for: a trick Adonis had learned in his long trek from Ontario to Winnipeg. They spent most of their time talking in hushed whispers, about the Principle, the Great Work, the Created, Pyros, and everything in between. Erwin had some familiarity with the principles of alchemy from his own explorations. But now Adonis was sharing everything he knew about true alchemy, the arcane science that could give life to lifeless tissue. He watched Erwin's eyes light up with wonder at the potential of Distillations, horror at the knowledge of Pandorans, and disgust as he realized the full extent of Amalgama's depravity. <br /> <br /> Erwin kept an ear out for news of Amalgama, and when they finished their investigation, Adonis and Erwin decided it was safe to return. Amalgama had suffered a serious set-back in Winnipeg, and from what Erwin could deduce from rumors, upper management had decided that the cost of rebuilding was too great, at least for the time being. Erwin and Adonis slipped back into the city. Adonis enjoyed the companionship while he could, but he knew that it could not last. He had to move on. He had explained the Roles to Erwin, and had felt nothing but regret as Erwin's eyes filled with heartbroken understanding. Two weeks after returning to Winnipeg, Erwin told Adonis that he understood why he had to move on, and encouraged him to. They parted ways, Erwin promising to help Adonis in any way he could. <br /> <br /> The Frozen Pilgrim had disappeared. When Adonis returned to Winnipeg, he heard rumors that she had fled north, towards Nunavut. He decided to follow her, damn the elements and Unborn, and try and find her. The news of her passing was everywhere- Created markings and scraps of paper left by passing pilgrims saying they had met a frozen Created in the area. Always two steps behind. Eventually, her tracks faded, and Adonis despaired in ever finding her, but then a traveling Extempore he met in Arviat told him of a frozen woman who had once been in Winnipeg, and had returned to that city a few weeks ago. Adonis turned back south, bound once more for the city of muddy waters. <br /> <br /> Adonis has still not found the Frozen Pilgrim, but other disquieting news has reached his ears: that there has been an upswing in Pandoran activity in the city since the raid on Amalgama: it seems that the laboratory reached deep into the earth, and misbegotten creatures had survived the fire, only to crawl out onto the surface in the days and weeks that followed.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I want the Frozen Pilgrim to be relevant to Adonis' story for a bit longer, a figure he tries to find and make contact with for the time being. Assuming Companion is complete, he's probably going to try and complete the Leader role from Aurum now. So the tidbits he's learned are: Amalgama is licking their wounds and is leaving Winnipeg alone for the time being, the Frozen Pilgrim is back in town, and the city is now swarming with Pandorans more than ever.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T07:49:57-08:00","id":1189222,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> alright, your timeskip is easiest to address so I'll start here first. These are all good things, and I really enjoy them. Mudbreaker is chasing the Aurora, right? No one has heard from her for a while. As far as they know, Mudbreaker is still up north. How did Mark 5 learn the Cathar's Path? Did he find an Athanor? Did Solomon teach him? Did the Scarlet Woman?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> Well, you could always make an Athanor of some kind or other, but I get the feeling that isn't what you have in mind. I mean, it would still be classified as an Athanor, but I don't think any of the existing ones make sense for Scout and what he wants to do. Take a look at the Azothic Object Merit, for example. I would consider applying a Condition or Tilt a one-dot trait. However, this would cost Experiences or Vitriol, or both. Whether you make one, and what you do with it, is entirely up to you. Now, if what he makes answers Scout's big question on Ascetic, and requires some level of sacrifice, it would also count for fulfilling the Universal Milestone of Divisio, what makes you different than humans. Humans cannot make alchemical objects through sheer force of will. It's a pretty stark reminder that you are a walking alchemical laboratory.<br /> <br /> In regards to the Concordance, you've pieced together enough clues from Highwinds' journal that you have managed to find a private personal blog of some kind from a member of the Concordance, and are currently corresponding with them. It appears as though this unknown Created spends <i>a lot </i>of time in the American Southwest around Arizona, and in Mexico, exploring the ruins of Mesoamerican civilizations.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"20770\" data-vbnamecard=\"20770\">Caius Wickersham</a> fear not, all the protagonists are coming back together, and you might be better prepared than most. After all, you've been in the city this whole time, you have the lay of the land. A lot can (and did) change in a year. The Canada Summer Games were held in the city last summer. There was a riotous explosion of the city's culture. Art events were better attended than ever, local sports teams are doing well, Folklorama and the Fringe Festival were huge events, as always. A politically conservative government came into provincial power and threatened to obliterate healthcare and education. A noted First Nations activist, Wab Kenew, became the head of the local NDP, and then it came out that he has an old domestic violence charge and that's lingered like a black cloud over him. Valentine's Day 2017 a bus driver was murdered for asking a passenger to get off the bus so that the driver could go home, because it was nearly 1AM. Fentanyl swept the streets leaving to numerous pleading radio PSAs. Busy, busy year.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> I really like your take, yes that absolutely fulfills Companion, because Erwin and Adonis had a fight over purely human things (Adonis lied to him) and not over the content of that interaction (that, you know, Adonis is an alchemical being). All the rumours are great, and I can see this going in extremely interesting directions, since I want to start introducing some of the other things that go bump in the night in Winnipeg. Pandorans on the loose cause problems for everyone.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> I've got your PM, and I'll respond there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T08:10:12-08:00","id":1189227,"title":"","content":"Basil will be taking the time to observe these actions, learning what he can from the unity the more positive elements provide and feeling the dread he experiences from those acts of selfishness he sees in humanity that disturbs him. Even the mutual selfishness of the bus driver and passenger (how much further did the guy need to go and was he able to go on his own?) gives him pause with humans. Looking into Kenew's past might be a nice distraction from hunting down Rambles and avoiding Pandorans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham","name":"Caius Wickersham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T08:34:35-08:00","id":1189235,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> <br /> Definitly still chasing the Aurora.<br /> Mark 5 was initiated by Solomon. After some in-depth talking, he stormed off, and tried going around in his fulfilled Role as Soldier for a day or two, but soon realized that he constantly found himself thinking about Earth's insightful advice, Solomon's words, Joshua's claims of a 'mission', his own abhorrent actions and guilt, and impurity. Villains, bad people, humans, Created, and impurity. What was the connection? He realized he <i>needed </i>to know.<br /> Finally, he returned to Solomon, confided his guilty Torment experience in him, and was taught the Cathar's Path.<br /> What he learned was confusing, strange, at odds with everything he'd stood for in places, but also weirdly fitting in some other places.<br /> And so, he became a low-rank mook, helping low-class criminals with their low-profile deeds. The money he earned was not important - the trust of his partners in crime was. Their willingness to share secrets about things they did and regretted was the highest currency. Learning how they thought, maybe even why they acted like this, was his goal.<br /> Taking part in their crimes was the only way he could think of getting this trust, because he had to realize that, yes, his body was strong, and he was resilient and stubborn, but his mind was weak. It put a <i>significant </i>dent into his 'Hero' attitude.<br /> <br /> As to why Solomon taught him the Path, he had no idea, because as far as he could tell, he was neither a promising disciple nor a successful Cathar.<br /> <br /> So, in comparison to last time, this is a more &quot;broken&quot; Mark: less proud, less strong, less focused, a bit aim- and directionless, less 'useful'.<br /> <br /> I would like it if Isla said &quot;Thanks&quot; for being rescued, which would resolve one of Mark 5's aspirations: Save someone's life and receive gratitude for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T15:18:22-08:00","id":1189294,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> Azothic object would be perfect for it, and an excellent spot to spend an xp. I was hoping to calcify an alembic or two before moving on, but it looks like I'll be well short of that as I move into quicksilver. Given his next role is Craftsman, I'd like to make it a tool of some sort. Maybe just hammer? Have it grant 9 again on his craft rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T15:31:26-08:00","id":1189298,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about how to translate it into this game as a rumor, but the Places of Interest section of Year Without a Summer is full of really cool stuff. I love that whole Era; even putting aside the Frankenstein stuff there's so much there to build a game around. Maybe something based on Der Popanz, ou's one of my favorite CofD characters just from the little snapshot presented. I wanna do a scavenger hunt for a vindictive agender puppet!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1189235#post1189235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And so, he became a low-rank mook, helping low-class criminals with their low-profile deeds. The money he earned was not important - the trust of his partners in crime was. Their willingness to share secrets about things they did and regretted was the highest currency. Learning how they thought, maybe even why they acted like this, was his goal.<br /> Taking part in their crimes was the only way he could think of getting this trust, because he had to realize that, yes, his body was strong, and he was resilient and stubborn, but his mind was weak. It put a <i>significant </i>dent into his 'Hero' attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Say it ain't so, Hero! That's a gut punch to see him falling like that. I'm excited for this, I wanna see what he and Earth have to say to each other now. Maybe now that he's off his pedestal, they can talk about what really happened to that stolen Vitriol...<br /> <br /> EDIT: other rumor ideas<ul><li>a touring band is in town, they look like <a href=\"http://bvbcomix.com/bandvsband/honey-vs-a-trip-outside-her-comfort-zone\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, and they're a bunch of lowlife licks hiding in plain sight as &quot;vampires&quot; onstage</li> <li>people were totally enthralled by a performance at the Fringe Festival that may have been a Changeling ritual</li> <li>a Bound &quot;boatman&quot; who gives off very strong con-man vibes has supposedly found a way into the underworld via the Red</li> </ul><br /> also deciding what to do about XP. I have enough to get to Azoth 4, and high Azoth was an original character goal, but I could also buy up Repute to 3 and boost Library, maybe get a Skill or Specialty (Drumming?) to reflect more mundane interests. I have exactly 2 Vitriol right now and can't decide if I want to calcify something from Metamorphosis or wait until I can boost Pilgrimage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 02-25-2018, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T05:58:38-08:00","id":1189388,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'd also like to spent 2 of Mark 5's 3 xp on getting Persuasion 1.<br /> Because I think this is a fair reflection of what he'd have learned in this past year on his path (also, without at least that, he has basically zero chance at getting anyone to open up to him =D)<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Yeah, that would be cool =D And yes, I hope Mark 5 will be a very sympathetic char this chapter ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T17:00:17-08:00","id":1189496,"title":"","content":"I feel seen: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/Yuri_Librarian/status/967159049446875136\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/Yuri_Librarian/s...59049446875136</a><br /> <br /> actual content: I've been reading through the IC and recruit threads to get characters and original concepts back in my head, really psyched to jump back in now.<br /> <br /> I can't wait for our throng to get to Arizona. I've been doodling ideas about Earth going to Sells, AZ to learn the O'odham language as a very Tammuz-y milestone. It would be a cool way to do the Companion Role, using Deception-Assimilation to create a false connection to their body's home community and getting a glimpse of what another life would have looked like. I like the Twilight Zone vibe of &quot;oh yeah, good old Cousin Whatsername, she's been here...oh, bout as long as anybody can remember&quot; as Wasteland and Disquiet slowly builds. Maybe even dealing with a protective local Awakened from Tucson, the only one who notices something is wrong.<br /> <br /> another edit to avoid double posting: I'm spending 5 Experiences on Azoth 3&gt;4, and 2 Vitriol to calcify Bestiae Facies. Earth has two shapes stored so far: a goose and a moose.<br /> <br /> Current Aspirations<ul><li>Join a branded throng</li> <li>See the Unholy play (un)live</li> <li>Find a way into the Underworld (long-term)</li> <li>Talk to someone else about what they have faith in (Elpis)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 02-27-2018, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T09:55:58-08:00","id":1190698,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> seems like a great Azothic Object to me, but bear in mind that the Craftsman Role isn't, necessarily, just about making physical objects.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> duly noted. Also, go ahead and give yourself a Beat for that Aspiration and replace it, because Isla definitely thanked Mark after the Amalgama incident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T15:34:27-08:00","id":1190826,"title":"","content":"No, but it's one I like for him moving forward from Ascetic, and it makes a really good transition point into that part of his life. I thought about going scientist first, but then we'd have to go back into Craftsman after this, which just didn't meet up really. He's finally made a thing, and realized why he's so different- now he needs to make things like humans do- though he does need a little help right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T01:12:21-08:00","id":1190919,"title":"","content":"I just jumped into the IC thread with an idea I'd had, but should we be posting that we're arriving at the Ramble or something? Or somebody can join Earth at the garden, something that gets PCs in the same place and talking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T17:54:30-08:00","id":1191182,"title":"","content":"It's alright for everyone to be doing their own thing detailing how they got back to the city and what's up with them. I'd kind of prefer that, actually. Little bit of a prologue character to character, but if everyone is ready I can jump straight to the Ramble.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20770-caius-wickersham\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"20770\" data-vbnamecard=\"20770\">Caius Wickersham</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode